{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys","id":909007,"title":"Are Solars the good guys?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T03:01:47-07:00","id":909007,"title":"Are Solars the good guys?","content":"Hello, noble peepsicles of assorted flavours. After searching deep within myself, and on this fine forum, I've been unable to find an answer to this simplest of questions. Are Solars the good guys?<br /> <br /> I've played exactly one session of Exalted, although I'm more familiar with the setting and mechanics, because A: I'm the only player in my group able to read the goddamn book apparently, and B: Our ST is a giant Exalted fanboy. I created a character in the expectation of !Heroic Endeavour Style! and !Innocent Saving Prana!, but after our first session, I'm finding that my party are... not the good guys. Maybe that's just the people I'm playing with, but we've got one devious snake-tongued trust-betraying sidereal-in-solar's-clothing, one Lawful Evil Bureaucrat, one straight-up rape-and-murder pirate and one ex-mercenary bent on killing every dishonourable employer he's ever had (does this count as good?). In the middle of this party, I'm playing... basically Jesus. Am I doing it wrong? Are they doing it wrong? Are we -supposed- to be actual Anathema, or is there simply something I'm missing?<br /> <br /> I really need help with this problem before Sunday if possible, because I like my character, but if evil Solars are totally legitimate, i'm going to have to roll up a new character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:23:21-07:00","id":909012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, noble peepsicles of assorted flavours. After searching deep within myself, and on this fine forum, I've been unable to find an answer to this simplest of questions. Are Solars the good guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer: no. The Solars are humans with power. They are just as good or bad, for some definition of those terms, as that implies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've played exactly one session of Exalted, although I'm more familiar with the setting and mechanics, because A: I'm the only player in my group able to read the goddamn book apparently, and B: Our ST is a giant Exalted fanboy. I created a character in the expectation of !Heroic Endeavour Style! and !Innocent Saving Prana!, but after our first session, I'm finding that my party are... not the good guys. Maybe that's just the people I'm playing with, but we've got one devious snake-tongued trust-betraying sidereal-in-solar's-clothing, one Lawful Evil Bureaucrat, one straight-up rape-and-murder pirate and one ex-mercenary bent on killing every dishonourable employer he's ever had (does this count as good?). In the middle of this party, I'm playing... basically Jesus. Am I doing it wrong? Are they doing it wrong? Are we -supposed- to be actual Anathema, or is there simply something I'm missing? </div> </div> </div>Short answer: Maybe. The game is open for you to be anything (and it's not surprising that those without investment in the setting play typically selfish or &quot;evil&quot; characters). If it's right for the group is another question entirely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really need help with this problem before Sunday if possible, because I like my character, but if evil Solars are totally legitimate, i'm going to have to roll up a new character. </div> </div> </div>Solars going out of control was the reason the Usurpation happened. It's absolutely legitimate. The question is if it's fun. It might be! In that case, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:30:27-07:00","id":909016,"title":"","content":"Evil Solars are just as legitimate as good Solars (and they can still save the world even, just in less... nice way), seems that there was some misunderstanding about what type of session you are going to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:37:51-07:00","id":909018,"title":"","content":"Some Solars are good. Some Solars are bad.<br /> There are 150 of them, after all.<br /> <br /> I think the books are written with the expectation that most people are going to make relatively good PCs (if more heroic warriors than Jesus), because that's what players tend to do (or at least, think they're doing).<br /> But there's no particular reason people have to make good characters.<br /> Same with DnD I guess, though since there's no objective measure of PC morality in Exalted, the ST can't really say &quot;no Evil characters please&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe talk to the ST and other players about what kind of game people want, good or bad (the ST may be as surprised as you). It's also possible of course, that the other players don't realise they're playing bad guys (I see this a lot). Or maybe they do, and love it, you know them better than I.<br /> <br /> (One note: Solars are written with the <i>imagery</i> of good guys. Shining gold paladins, rightful kings, chosen by God to go forth and smite evil... but the original writers deliberately didn't actually make any rules that said you had to be good, or got some benefit for it: it was a bit of a deconstruction of the whole paladin/returning king thing, though I don't think that's something the current writers are so interested in)<br /> <br /> <br /> A good few years ago, having played a lot of Dragonblood and one Celestial game, I decided to run my own Solar game. I wanted to do something different from jaded aristocrats oppress the Threshold once again. And my friends played, well, not exactly moral paragons (they were PCs after all), but certainly characters who considered themselves heroes. Sure, the Lunar ex-monk slept with prostitutes, and the Dawn caste wanted to conquer the area, but when villagers were being attacked by zombies or oppressed by evil Kings you could rely on them to try to save the innocents and be big damn heroes.<br /> <br /> Then, I decided to try running a Solar game for some other friends, so they could play too. I was utterly shocked when local villagers begged them for help from a beastman horde, and the Pirate and Mercenary said &quot;how much can you pay us? Nothing? Nope, we'll leave you to die.&quot;<br /> Because Exalted has no moral system, you can play an evil Solar if you want. It was just jarring. But again, I guess that's the same as with most role-playing games that let you make a wide variety of PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-07-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:43:05-07:00","id":909019,"title":"","content":"Solars are here to save a world that has fallen into corruption and ruin.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat can mean one is Jesus, but also Oda Nobunaga.<br /> <br /> On the face of it, the other characters you've described sound like they're still trying to do or build things that can be useful to people or the world, so I'd say it's all valid. If you can be okay with playing with them, I'd say the contrast between characters can create some good dramatic tension. If the difference is something you're not having fun with, I'd say you should talk it out with the other players, and see if some things can't be compromised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:43:52-07:00","id":909020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909012#post909012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars going out of control was the reason the Usurpation happened. It's absolutely legitimate. The question is if it's fun. It might be! In that case, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I thought that the Solars -went- bad, rather than -started- bad. If some Solars are just wrong'uns, I'm having some serious issues disagreeing with the Bronze faction.<br /> <br /> My quote button isn't working properly, so I'll just reply to everyone else -<br /> <br /> Yeah, I guess. In discussion, everyone (except the pirate) seemed to have much more noble character concepts and honestly, I'm having trouble seeing how the rape-and-pillage pirate could ever save the day. He's a (literal) giant day-ruiner. I think I'll talk to my GM and craft an evil Jesus for the event that playing a good guy in a bad party becomes unbearable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 06-07-2016, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T03:56:43-07:00","id":909022,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Sidereal-pretending-to-be-a-Solar, bureaucrat, and ex-mercenary out to punish dishonourable employers may not have been intended to be evil. They might have just been a bad influence on each other. It has only been one session, you said.<br /> The other one sounds just like a bad guy though.<br /> <br /> I will say though, if you're playing a Jesus-esque character, not many groups of PCs are going to be good enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:09:28-07:00","id":909025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909020#post909020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I thought that the Solars -went- bad, rather than -started- bad. If some Solars are just wrong'uns, I'm having some serious issues disagreeing with the Bronze faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm not even saying it's one or the other. I'm sure it's both, and other things besides.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I guess. In discussion, everyone (except the pirate) seemed to have much more noble character concepts and honestly, I'm having trouble seeing how the rape-and-pillage pirate could ever save the day. He's a (literal) giant day-ruiner. I think I'll talk to my GM and craft an evil Jesus for the event that playing a good guy in a bad party becomes unbearable. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:09:49-07:00","id":909026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909022#post909022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Sidereal-pretending-to-be-a-Solar, bureaucrat, and ex-mercenary out to punish dishonourable employers may not have been intended to be evil. They might have just been a bad influence on each other. It has only been one session, you said.<br /> The other one sounds just like a bad guy though.<br /> <br /> I will say though, if you're playing a Jesus-esque character, not many groups of PCs are going to be good enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I might have set the bar for high horses a bit..well, high. How many games do you need to craft &quot;backup evil jesus&quot; for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:14:09-07:00","id":909029,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly the Devs for this edition deliberately didn't mention or picture any of the cannon solars who were straight-up villains, and have said that each solar carries at least the potential for good in their character. That being said if your ST favors a darker and grittier creation that is his prerogative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:22:11-07:00","id":909033,"title":"","content":"... Wow. I'm kinda surprised at how many people came out in favour of 'Yeah, Solars can be evil'.<br /> <br /> Roanas, while I agree that Evil Solars are a thing, the particular evil Solars you describe feel.... weird to me. No matter what their moral stance, Solars are supposed to be epic impressive people. They're not just a mid level paper pusher, they're the Vizir who tangles up whole courts in their scheming. Not just a swordsman, but one of the greatest in the land. Most of the canon Solar villains were similarly epic in scope, or working on it. Havesh the Vanisher wasn't just some thug, he was a nightmare to Varangians everywhere. Your guys... kinda sound more like an old school evil D&amp;D party to me. Could be me, could be the short description, not sure<br /> <br /> Might be worth asking the ST what he expects in a chronicle, and what he expects of Solars. 2E had them chosen by abstract skill; the greatest human beings in XYZ. 3E blurs that by having anyone be theoretically eligable, but they have to be chosen by the Sun directly. If your group is running with 3E fluff on this, I'm struggling to see why 'rape and murder pirate' was Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:32:55-07:00","id":909037,"title":"","content":"I agree that Solars can be evil and evil Solars can make great villains, but as a play experience I find that they tend to be at worst anti-heroes. This is in large part because of their place in the setting, naturally opposed to a rapacious empire run by aristocratic jerks who want them dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:34:58-07:00","id":909038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909033#post909033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havesh the Vanisher wasn't just some thug, he was a nightmare to Varangians everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, wealthy and corrupt Varangians everywhere. Havesh insists that he has no interest in targeting or exploiting the already downtrodden for purely pragmatic reasons, but he insists that repeatedly and at the drop of a hat, which could be read as trying a bit too hard.<br /> <br /> Also, the one time he didn't kill for money or personal protection was a man who violently abused a casteless Varangian out of nowhere just to make a point.<br /> <br /> For that pirate, I would ask who the violence is being targeted at; by the old world justice logic of some parts of the setting, some people just need their days ruined.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:38:55-07:00","id":909042,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Croakamancer for the most part, while the player is free play what they wish it is difficult to see how some of those guys Exalted... <br /> That being said I never actually saw the Usurpation being at all about the Solars being 'evil' a word which comes across as really silly for this setting where you have a hilarious number of factions that flat out want kill/destroy literally everything. The Usurpation's justification came from a large number of Solars being insane which by extension led to gaps of incompetence and Creation itself being at risk. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are more than content to support a competent tyrant (like the empress) whose entire ruling style is basically domestic peace at the price of untold millions suffering from their activities abroad because they dont have to worry about her destroying Creation out of insane boredom (even 'sane' Solars have little to no self-preservation instincts when in the face of their own curiousity).<br /> <br /> The more important question you should be asking yourself is how your character was special and exceptional enough that the literal god of awesome still made them Exalt, morality should be a secondary priority. But boring people that dont seem like they would do something awesome woth their powers are highly unlikely to exalt.<br /> <br /> YMMV ultimately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-07-2016, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:50:23-07:00","id":909044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909020#post909020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My quote button isn't working properly</div> </div> </div> </div>Quotes work a bit weirdly on this forum software. You can quote a single post just by clicking the Quote button and it will appear in the text box at the bottom of the page. However, if you want to quote several posts you have to mark each post by clicking the Quote button and then click the Post Reply button at the top of the page (and no, for some damn reason it doesn't work with the Post Reply button at the bottom). There should be a paranthesis with the number of quoted post as well, so it'll look like &quot;Post Reply (3)&quot; for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-07-2016, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T04:56:30-07:00","id":909048,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the pirate exalted by being just the best goddamn pirate in Creation. He wept when he had no more worlds to conquer, and the Unconquered Sun said &quot;Here, try the entire of Creation&quot;.<br /> <br /> The sneaky, devious git-in-a-bag Twilight was the first son of a noble DB household, and in performing great feats and whatnot to support his DB exaltation, he accidentally Exalted wrong.<br /> <br /> The bureaucrat... I'm not even sure. I have no sodding clue how he popped. I'm going to have to ask his player.<br /> <br /> The vengeful ex-merc was just great at killing people, and exalted when he realised he was killing the wrong people and went on his murder-quest.<br /> <br /> Except for the bureaucrat, those all seem to me like reasonable reasons to Exalt, which seems (based on the majority of opinions given so far) like they -deserved- their exaltations at least. I'll have to re-evaluate how I thought of Solar Exaltation, it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:07:55-07:00","id":909052,"title":"","content":"I've Always went with the interpretation that Solars are Heroes, in the Classical Sense. David and Goliath are both Heroes.. but only one is framed in a good Light.<br /> <br /> Sephiroth and Cloud are both Heroes, but one is Selfish and the other Grows into it.<br /> <br /> It all depends on the origin/definition point of them becoming a Hero. Cloud always wanted to be, Sephiroth just was and was expected to be. (Yes I know that Sephiroth is only a Soldier.. but Still to the common people he was a Hero)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:15:13-07:00","id":909057,"title":"","content":"My take on it is that Exaltation makes you more of what you are...except that nobody is really &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil.&quot; There's just the actions you take.<br /> <br /> So you could be a killer-of-petty-thieves, be blessed by the Sun, and either decide that you could kill <b>more</b> petty thieves everywhere, or you could aim to kill the greatest thieves of all; those who stole your future in a past life, the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> So nobody is really, inherently good. Your character can act good, and do good things, but you have to <b>work</b> for it. You have to work for everything worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:21:53-07:00","id":909059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909048#post909048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the pirate exalted by being just the best goddamn pirate in Creation. He wept when he had no more worlds to conquer, and the Unconquered Sun said &quot;Here, try the entire of Creation&quot;.<br /> <br /> The sneaky, devious git-in-a-bag Twilight was the first son of a noble DB household, and in performing great feats and whatnot to support his DB exaltation, he accidentally Exalted wrong.<br /> <br /> The bureaucrat... I'm not even sure. I have no sodding clue how he popped. I'm going to have to ask his player.<br /> <br /> The vengeful ex-merc was just great at killing people, and exalted when he realised he was killing the wrong people and went on his murder-quest.<br /> <br /> Except for the bureaucrat, those all seem to me like reasonable reasons to Exalt, which seems (based on the majority of opinions given so far) like they -deserved- their exaltations at least. I'll have to re-evaluate how I thought of Solar Exaltation, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classically, that's correct. That's how Exaltation worked in Ex2. It... caaan still work like that, as I understand it, but the overall intent is that every Solar was chosen specifically by TUS, and that TUS is... at least VAGUELY a good guy. Like, he'll sign off to the bold, the daring, the charismatic.... but the more gitish people might make him stop and pause.<br /> <br /> *shrug* There's a lot of personal preference and different fluff ideas on this point, so its something possibly worthy of some group discussion. I'll say that I'm really not used to seeing Solars skew <i>that </i>evil, and my current main concept is a Night Caste Thieves Guild Leader. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:23:37-07:00","id":909060,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem to be in the case of this thread, but I think the question touches on the question of whether a person's characteristics can be irrelevant to the question of whether or not they're doing some good in the world.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying in the sense of &quot;evil person who ruthlessly pursues brutal means of achieving a noble goal, or is hard enough to make the tough decisions&quot;, I'm saying where the associations between who you are and how you govern are non-existent.<br /> <br /> For instance, there's Frederick William I, King in Prussia, father of Frederick the Great (one of the greatest military minds in European history). As a ruler, he was an autocrat, but highly effective and even equitable, revising tax codes to something more comprehensible and reasonable, building schools and hospitals and encouraging education, resettling land depopulated by plague, ordering reclamation of marshland, stockpiling grain for the public good, and developing a highly comprehensive code for the civil service, which did not suffer laxity in any officials. Although he drilled the kingdom's army to an extremely high quality, he himself hardly ever pursued wars, seeing them as a wasteful extravagance. In his own right, he was reported to be a highly diligent administrator, who worked long hours, lived an austere, unostentatious lifestyle (to the point of limiting use of candles in order to save on money), and is even said to have paid his own consumer tax. As kings go, he was probably not exactly what one would call oppressive.<br /> <br /> As a person, he was known to be brutal to the point of outright sadism, given to violent tempers and unforgiving of even small discrepancies. Few people experienced this more than prince Frederick, whose interest in things like music and literature were regarded as decadent and unmanly by a father who wanted to shape him into an effective civil and military leader. Frederick was held to a harsh regime of education and military exercises, and would be beaten for the slightest failing or defiance; he was reportedly punished in this manner for things like being thrown from his horse, or wearing gloves in cold weather. The king's treatment was such that the prince actually once attempted to flee into exile with his friend and tutor, and when they were captured, Frederick was forced to watch his friend's execution, which is said to have made him faint and experience hallucinations for days afterwards; some think Frederick William would have killed his son as well if he thought the Reichstag would have let him get away with it (at the time, Prussia was still under a lot of Imperial power).<br /> <br /> So the point I'm making with all of this is that you can have a person, whether as a ruler or exercising their skill or power in some other way, who does great, helpful, even just things, while being a complete heel in their personal life and relationships. I don't think that even necessarily entails hypocrisy.<br /> <br /> You might also be able to have the converse, but I'd say that's a bit more precarious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:25:17-07:00","id":909062,"title":"","content":"A brief interlude; here's the Ex3 passage on 'who Exalts Solar'?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Solar Exaltation is unpredictable, though a few generalizations can be made. Solars are often men and women who have already accomplished great things and displayed excellence in some discipline or other. This isn\u2019t universal\u2014 sometimes a Solar is simply a person of enormous potential who has never had the opportunity to exercise it, or who is possessed of greatness of spirit. Although it\u2019s rare for cruel blackguards to gain the Unconquered Sun\u2019s blessing, there\u2019s little consistency in the morality of those that are Chosen. Many consider themselves righteous, but their definitions of righteous behavior vary widely enough to have brought the Solar Exalted to war in the past\u2014and will again. </div> </div> </div>.... Dear me, that's not helpful. :P Could they have made the waters any muddier?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:33:40-07:00","id":909065,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's particularly unclear: Solars are people who are either highly accomplished, or have unrealised potential; Solars are not often absolutely terrible, but there's a lot of variety in their morals, especially in a manner that brings them into conflict.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat else is there?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:39:21-07:00","id":909068,"title":"","content":"The potential vs skill thing's fine. But the morality thing is just frecking muddled. They can be moral... or they can not be! The lack of definitive terms means it's kinda worthless in this situation: you can say 'cruel blackguards are rare' as justification for Solars skew good, but then you can use the rest of it for a more humanist shades of grey interpretation, and the language overall saying blackguard Solars are possible means it's hard to point to it as evidence for... much of anything really.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that's wrong exactly: there's some validity to not tying down what Solars can or can't be.I'm just saying it's not much use for anyone trying to work out if a given concept fits as a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:41:45-07:00","id":909072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Solars the good guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Often enough.For certain values of good.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T05:48:07-07:00","id":909075,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Basically Jesus&quot; in a ragtag band of thieves and brigands is totally viable. You just need to come up with a good reason for him to be there.<br /> <br /> Maybe he sees the good in people, and is trying to steer these guys into being the genuine heroes he knows they can be. He might wind up being the Colossus in a team of Deadpools, but are you going to let that stop you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:17:23-07:00","id":909094,"title":"","content":"Are Solars the good guys?<br /> Not by definition, but players often point them in that direction. Solars are by definition <i>great </i>first and foremost and <i>good</i> often comes second---even if it's a very close second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:19:46-07:00","id":909096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909068#post909068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> you can say 'cruel blackguards are rare' as justification for Solars skew good, but then you can use the rest of it for a more humanist shades of grey interpretation, and the language overall saying blackguard Solars are possible means it's hard to point to it as evidence for... much of anything really.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI think &quot;cruel blackguard&quot; is meant to be something a bit more specific than general morality, especially considering that there is a line right after saying that there is not much apparent moral consistency.<br /> <br /> Like, writing off people who resemble Idi Amin almost entirely is not a comprehensive statement of &quot;Solars are good&quot;, it's just a statement that the greatest extremes of evil or similar character deficiency are probably not valid.<br /> <br /> But while still likely including figures such as Oda Nobunaga or Genghis Khan, who I personally would not characterise as cruel blackguards at the same time as I would not dream of calling them particularly nice.<br /> <br /> At the same time, it's pointing out that even when there <i>are</i> Solars who could be considered reasonably moral (if only by themselves, and yes, that is a significant distinction because no, not every monster regards themselves as the heroes of their own stories), that doesn't prevent them from coming into conflict because reasonably moral people can still have notably different world views, as a moral exercise or otherwise, or because different (and arguably valid) standards of moral behaviour can be difficult to reconcile.<br /> <br /> Like, without speaking of that particular pirate character of whom I know little, you could have a Solar modelled off of Francis Drake, raiding shipping and sacking ports in the name of the righteous cause of defending the homeland and tweaking the noses of the greedy and tyrannical empire, who comes into conflict with the Solar who views all forms of piracy as rank criminality and that it is righteous to destroy them (which itself can be ambiguous, depending on the background of any given pirates, which can include impoverished coastal communities and suddenly unemployed privateers).<br /> <br /> But I do grant that this all depends on how expansive one reads the term &quot;cruel blackguard&quot;, and even then, I think the context of the overall text might be cause for some adjustments of that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:21:13-07:00","id":909099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think &quot;Basically Jesus&quot; in a ragtag band of thieves and brigands is totally viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now thinking of Firefly. Though there I guess most of the thieves and brigands were good deep down, so were open to Book's influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyhow, perhaps that can be the test of Rowanas's characters true heroism. Can he convince the others to become more good?<br /> <br /> (You know, Solar Jesus has been suggested to me as a concept before, or Lunar Aslan of course, but I wouldn't dare play it: I don't think I could play a perfect person consistently. And I wouldn't let my players play it either, because I don't think they could manage it! So, if you do manage to play it well, kudos.)<br /> <br /> <br /> When we started (so, so long ago) our Celestial game, our group included a psychotic one-eyed Lunar who murdered Realm soldiers in their sleep, a less psychotic Lunar... who killed slavers and ate their hearts (and had prior to the game killed and eaten several people such as a teenage girl and an old woman), a Mongol sorcerer who wanted to conquer the world, and two soldiers who loved, well, conquering stuff. After one of them died, he was replaced by a naive street kid Night. Over time, the Night's influence softened all the other PCs, and stopped them really wanting to conquer anyone (although one of them later ran off to become a villain). The Lunar (now his wife) hardly ever kills anyone (well, except the occasional monarch/tyrant).<br /> The group is almost pacifistic, under his influence.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you definately shouldn't change your character, but this is a possibility. I'd talk to the other players and see if they realise how evil their PCs come off as. In my experience, a lot of players think their PCs are far more heroic than they appear to others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the main point that everyone's arguing about<b></b>: I'm broadly in agreement with this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree that Solars can be evil and evil Solars can make great villains, but as a play experience I find that they tend to be at worst anti-heroes. This is in large part because of their place in the setting, naturally opposed to a rapacious empire run by aristocratic jerks who want them dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking I find them to be vaguely on the good side, because they're opposed to the Realm, the Abyssals, the Infernals, etc. And most of them come from ordinary backgrounds, so are generally up for protecting humanity from supernatural threats.<br /> <br /> But that's not the same as saying &quot;only good people exalt as Solars&quot;. (Which would be a horrendous system: I mean, how would you enforce that, mechanically?) (Some might point out that it could also just be people with the potential for good... but that's 100% of human beings. Even sociopaths.) They're just as likely to be as xenophobic or greedy as anyone else.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm agreeing with Isator here a bit: to do what the Solars were created for, save the world from monsters, you don't have to be a saint.<br /> <br /> Of course, once they've booted out the Realm, stopped the Abyssals and Infernals... what then? Conquering humanity and ruling as kings, perhaps? That's kind of the issue that happened before.<br /> <br /> Honestly I find the way some people want one splat to be &quot;the good guys&quot; very confusing. Surely individuals are good or bad, not large groups of people with the same appearance? Isn't it what you do (and perhaps think) that makes you good, not who you are? Shouldn't it be up to the players to try to make a character who acts in a good way, not the game saying &quot;these guys are the good guys&quot;. I mean, unless we want to be running a deconstructionist approach like 1st and 2nd ed sometimes did (and sometimes forgot to do), where the game says &quot;Solars are the good guys!&quot; and then shows some examples of bad Solars to make you question whether a group of this kind can be said to be inherently &quot;the good guys&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:34:38-07:00","id":909109,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much what the Gold faction wants the Solars to do tho, rule creation again but this time, they want to make sure that they are the proper advisors and educate them in the way, they think, they should rule creation. Some Gold faction members in 1e, had some cool ideas on how to deal with Solars, they sent them on missions to places with more and more dangers, a couple of gold faction sidereals believe that Solars essentially need to have challenges all the time or when they get bored...that's when the problems start coming.<br /> <br /> Solars come from the brand of Greek Heroism. Greek heroes were never about being good guys or bad guys, it was always about the deeds, epic tasks etc...Hercules was hardly a good guy compared to his version in Disney.<br /> <br /> But well at least from what we know in the podcast...things are going to get better before they get a lot worse...so some great dangers are coming in the horizon, who knows what would be stance of most factions, group, gods and people in creation, when they would need the Solars for help.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:37:45-07:00","id":909110,"title":"","content":"Yes. Solars are the good guys. Source: They glow yellow. <i>Yellow</i>. Obviously the most moral color.<br /> <br /> More seriously, though. Obviously nobody is axiomatically good or evil. That said, the Celestials in general and Solars in particular tend to be closer to what we'd consider conventionally good. I suspect this is even more true in Third Edition; Solars are personally selected by the Unconquered Sun and generally represent, at least when they Exalt, something that he considers virtuous or worth Exalting.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun himself is of course not axiomatically good, so you have to take this with a grain of salt... but he's not awful, and I suspect if you wrote down the morality and thought-process of the various in-setting entities with their own Exalted, and had people rank them based on how good they are or whatever, the UCS would rank at or near the top. There would be some people who'd hate him, people who would prefer the Maidens or Luna or whatever, but overall he's the closest fit for what we'd consider good, and his Exalted <i>generally</i> skew a bit more towards that, just like the Lunars tend a bit more towards survival-of-the-fittest and Sidereals skew a bit more towards fatalism and utilitarianism and What Must Be Done and all that.<br /> <br /> You can have awful Solars, but usually you would have to answer the question of &quot;what did the Unconquered Sun see in this guy?&quot;, which implies that even totally horrible Solars have a degree more focus on the fact that they had the possibility to be someone better, or that they have or had some aspect to them that the Unconquered Sun found appealing.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Some Solars are terrible, but almost all Solars have at least the <i>potential</i> to be good.<br /> <br /> (Of course, to the extent that Exalted is humanist -- and I think it is, especially with the Solars as the central Exalt type -- this is true about all the Exalted, too; but Solars exemplify it most directly and have it most clearly as a theme.)<br /> <br /> Like, the central theme of Solars draws heavily on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xeW-AMP87PM\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. And they often fall short of that, but it's still core to what they are. They were created to be humanity's champions and teachers, the people who scout new horizons and find common ground among humanity's disparate parts; they weren't created to be its tyrants, no matter how awful they sometimes behaved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:45:37-07:00","id":909114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Solars the good guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>From their own perspective, most Solars are the good guys, sure. And, from the in-setting perspective of a savage Creation where human life is cheap and human rights don't exist, many of them could be. What's a little ultra-violence and general thuggery when you were Chosen by the Most High to guide Creation?<br /> <br /> From our 21st century, socially-conscious, being-vegan-makes-me-morally-superior outlook? Fuck no! Even most of the canon Circle, given to us as models of Solar-dom, are horrible people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've played exactly one session of Exalted, although I'm more familiar with the setting and mechanics, because A: I'm the only player in my group able to read the goddamn book apparently, and B: Our ST is a giant Exalted fanboy. I created a character in the expectation of !Heroic Endeavour Style! and !Innocent Saving Prana!, but after our first session, I'm finding that my party are... not the good guys. Maybe that's just the people I'm playing with, but we've got one devious snake-tongued trust-betraying sidereal-in-solar's-clothing, one Lawful Evil Bureaucrat, one straight-up rape-and-murder pirate and one ex-mercenary bent on killing every dishonourable employer he's ever had (does this count as good?). In the middle of this party, I'm playing... basically Jesus. Am I doing it wrong? Are they doing it wrong? Are we -supposed- to be actual Anathema, or is there simply something I'm missing? </div> </div> </div>This is a problem of mismatched expectations, not a problem of &quot;Who is playing Exalted right?&quot; The only version of Exalted that matters at your table is the one your group wants to play. With that in mind, it sounds like you arrived at the table believing one thing, and everyone else arrived believing another thing. I suggest asking for a brief OC discussion before the next game to figure out what people were expecting, and what they want. You might find the players with &quot;evil&quot; characters actually prefer more noble PCs, but thought they needed to fit into the setting.<br /> <br /> Also, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4086_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4086\" data-vbnamecard=\"4086\">Croakamancer</a> that overall your PC groups sounds like hacky DnD Evil characters than Solar Exalts.<br /> <br /> More broadly, though, I think this is one place 2E communicated more clearly and effectively. The passage Croak posted above accomplishes the Ex3 design goal of leaving things open, but seems to fail at conveying the design goal of most Solars starting &quot;good-ish,&quot; as Holden mentioned at one point. I'm using quotes for good and evil a fair bit because they are vague terms with an axiomatic connotation, and that irks me to no end. One man's sinner is another man's saint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo 06-07-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:47:50-07:00","id":909117,"title":"","content":"Wow, lots and lots of points made here. I've decided on a course of action 3 times in the course of this thread, and I might still have time to change my mind. I'm glad I posted this, because it's spawned some good discussions. Keep going!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:10:08-07:00","id":909139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909099#post909099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course, once they've booted out the Realm, stopped the Abyssals and Infernals... what then? Conquering humanity and ruling as kings, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any issue one has with that depends on the kind of king, I think.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike how I described Frederick William I of Prussia; you could do a lot worse.<br /> <br /> Or you could do somewhat ambiguously worse, such as Louis XIV of France, where exactly how oppressive he was depended a bit on what demographic of society you lived in. There's a ruler who brought a lot of stability and efficiency to what had previously been an extremely tumultuous nation, but also enacted some extremely harsh measures against Protestants. Apparently, not even as a religious issue, just an autocratic one; it supposedly offended the Sun King's sensibilities for there to be this notable lack of uniformity in his dominion.<br /> <br /> It's all just a case of how saving the world can legitimately include working towards and building things intended to change it.<br /> <br /> And even if you have vision and mean well, that doesn't make any of your conflicts unambiguous. Hamilton's mercantile and industrial vision of a United States with a strong federal government versus Jefferson's value of a nation of largely independent farmers with minimal government oversight or interference; which one is good? Which one is bad? What do people want, or need? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's kind of the issue that happened before.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find the Usurpation to be best written when it's ambiguous enough for people to use their own imagination to fill in what the Solars were actually doing that was so offensive, so it can be adjusted for taste.<br /> <br /> Still, speaking for myself, I've generally found the idea of &quot;Solars became bad to the extent one would associate with, say, Genghis Khan&quot; to create a logical inconsistency, and anything approaching &quot;Solars were bad because they were ruling things, and rulers are inevitably bad&quot; to rather undermine the thesis of the game.<br /> <br /> I mean... not talking about anybody in this thread or forum specifically, just a sentiment I've seen expressed and want to bring up for the sake of a point: I get the attraction of something that approaches a more comic book superhero image of &quot;saves the world but doesn't really have any opinions on it, except maybe for other superpowered stuff*&quot;, and Exalted is perfectly serviceable for games in which people play that. Just, in a forum of discussion, I'm going to attempt to argue some of the points on intellectual grounds, both in general and for any particular image the game might try to develop.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I think of occasions in which Batman or Iron Man are written as going off of the deep end with instituting measures intended to seize control of something, but these still tend to be targeted at gimmicky stuff like other superheroes or alien invasion threats or the like, rather than, say, issues with excessive capitalism or incompetent government.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T07:11:51-07:00","id":909141,"title":"","content":"James Bond is a remorseless killer, a seducer of women, a blunt instrument of death, imperialism, cruelty, and colonialism.<br /> <br /> And yet, he could be a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T08:12:23-07:00","id":909174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909141#post909141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">James Bond is a remorseless killer, a seducer of women, a blunt instrument of death, imperialism, cruelty, and colonialism.<br /> <br /> And yet, he could be a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elias Tremalion from 2E is a bald-faced Bond send up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T09:58:23-07:00","id":909241,"title":"","content":"Solars are big, not physically (although many are this too), but they have big plans, big ideas, big impacts, they dream big, they think big, and they go big. This often makes them look like good guys because frankly Creation is in desperate need of such. Furthermore Solars have a lot of inherited enemies that are either attempting to destroy the world, cruel and oppressive tyrants, or mind bogglingly wrong in how they go about things. So it's very easy for them to become heroes by default, not because of any inherent virtue, but because a lot of people are worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11837-a-not-quite-simple-soul","name":"A Not Quite Simple Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:16:26-07:00","id":909250,"title":"","content":"Solars can be evil because they are just humans who did heroic things. They are modeled after the paragon of virtue, but that doesn't mean they all have to be one. Examples of Night castes in 1e and 2e included things like serial killers stalking the streets.<br /> <br /> Theoretically The Punisher could even be a Solar. The Kingpin? Bureaucracy supernalwith, dip larceny, brawl and resistance for combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's more interesting for the setting of Solars aren't all Good Guys. Players who only accept solars as good people pigeon hole themselves out of fun characteristics.<br /> <br /> A selfish, greedy person can shape and change and save the world as well as any other. After all, all their stuff is in that world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 06-07-2016, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:23:33-07:00","id":909257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Am I doing it wrong? Are they doing it wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>No to both questions. I know that sounds contradictory but hear me out. Solars, and really Exalted in general are based on the Classical idea of heroes, Pulp Fantasy and the occasional dash of modern superheroics.<br /> So it's entirely possible to play a cutthroat rat bastard and literally jesus. It's entirely possible that the rat bastard was a predecessor of literally jesus, or vice versa, thanks to the way Exaltations work. Exaltation is a bit nuts that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:33:52-07:00","id":909265,"title":"","content":"I take a slightly non-canon view of Exaltations. Rather than asking if a character is heroic enough, I ask why the Unconquered Sun needs this particular hero at this point in time. What attracted the Sun to notice you? And why you, here, now? We have to remember that he is virtuous in almost every sense. He won't exalt someone because they are the best torturer in the kingdom. He won't exalt someone who is the laughable parody of chaotic evil. <br /> <br /> He will exalt Xanatos. He will exalt a conquerer. He will exalt a destroyer of armies. He will exalted a thief. He will exalt an assassin. But he won't exalt any of these things without a better reason than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T10:48:57-07:00","id":909278,"title":"","content":"I admit I wasn't quite expecting that from the title, but I'm glad to have found and read it.<br /> <br /> Things I'm Echoing: No, none of you are doing it wrong, Solars are super-powered humans but they'restill <i>human</i>, and you don't have to swap out your Walking Messiah for Evil Messiah unless you really feel like you're causing party friction.<br /> <br /> So yes, Solars can be good guys. I often play them as such, because I just prefer playing good guys. I play the Twilight who wants to safeguard his home, I play the Dawn that Exalted by standing between a village and a horde of Raksha, from dusk until dawn. I play the wandering Twilight who just wants to feed people.<br /> <br /> But sometimes, well... They can be heroes of another story, and sometimes the story is a bit grittier than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:13:51-07:00","id":909301,"title":"","content":"I'd like to say no. I would really *like* to just say that, and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> However, disregarding my preference and, being totally honest, I think the original premise is probably (from way back First Edition) that they weren't the &quot;Good Guys&quot; so much as *some* of them, at least, were &quot;Good&quot; and crucially, that Solars that were &quot;Good&quot; could really make it stick and change the world. (While the &quot;Good&quot; men and women in other groups, like the Dragonblooded, probably couldn't, because the opposition was just too huge for their power to cope with).<br /> <br /> That seems more or less the same overtone in 3e, but with more overtones of their god, the Unconquered Sun, being a &quot;Good Guy&quot;.<br /> <br /> So Solars can be &quot;Good&quot; and Solars can be &quot;Bad&quot;. But if a Solar is &quot;Good&quot;, he or she is the &quot;Only Hope For Mankind&quot;.<br /> <br /> (While another premise of the game is probably more, if you're &quot;Good&quot; and not a Solar, what does that really amount to? Who really cares? Because only the Solars have the chance to actually effect real change in the world.)<br /> <br /> Does that make sense? (The above is probably a bit full on for a total new fan. But maybe not.)<br /> <br /> (This stuff probably got lost in the huge enthusiasm among the early Exalted fans from the traditional White Wolfe fanbase, for totally deconstructing the narrative of the Chosen Ones who are the Only Chance For Mankind to Save The World. <br /> <br /> Which is a narrative I will gladly deconstruct every time it turns up, given my druthers. But Exalted the game doesn't really run on my druthers! And really, it there are other things like Godbound that get closer to avoiding this premise entirely, so it's not that big a deal.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:25:29-07:00","id":909311,"title":"","content":"To get right to the heart of it: this whole topic is not really an in-fiction concern. &quot;Are solars the good guys&quot; is an interesting question, but really, bears no impact on the table of play if the issues with good guys and bad guys are group cohesion. You can go on and on about philosophy, the nature of good and evil, blah blah blah, but in the case of an actual practical need? The answer is a simple &quot;Solars are only as good as that specific game requires them to be&quot;. This is not a question best answered with canon history (which almost always ends badly and pointlessly as a discussion) or philosophy of human nature, but instead simple practicality.<br /> <br /> That's a long way of saying &quot;Ask your ST&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T11:34:20-07:00","id":909321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909311#post909311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a long way of saying &quot;Ask your ST&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My suspicion is that you will find fewer games going with evil Solar PCs than Abyssals, Infernals or even Dragon-Bloods. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:33:52-07:00","id":909369,"title":"","content":"In addition to everything that was mentioned above about Solars and their morality and how a Solar is chosen...there is one other thing in the books that is worth mentioning for a young Solar: Essence Fever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Commanding Essence is a heady experience. It\u2019s not like speaking an incantation, turning a key, or \ufb02ipping a card. To be aware of Essence is to feel\u2014to always feel\u2014a new part of yourself, a part that is alive and active and burning with power. The Essence of the Exalted is as much a part of them as their blood or thoughts or breath, and young Exalts ache to use it.<br /> [...]<br /> If greatness is in the nature of the Solar Exalted, then their Essence pushes them to seize that greatness now. It\u2019s neither irresistible nor insurmountable, even for the very young\u2014 but the urge is there.<br /> [...]<br /> the voice that speaks out and urges him onward, to glory, to victory, to more. </div> </div> </div>Solars are powerfully driven to do great things...to reach out and grasp the world...to test their might against it. This is often why Solars can end up looking like heroes...they may take on the attacking horde not because they want to save the villagers...but because the horde is <i>there</i>, and they <i>can</i> take it on.<br /> <br /> Of course, we also have this little tidbit from a sidebar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To a Lawgiver, channeling Solar Essence brings a myriad of feelings and sensations. It is a kind of pure cosmic transcendence that is the order of the divine. It is soaring triumph and limitless joy; it is the harmony of all things, a song that lilts and lifts the soul, and the hum of raw, limitless power; it is a making and unmaking of the self, and an ecstasy of understanding. </div> </div> </div>This can be taken to imply that channeling Solar Essence has something of an effect on the person using it. It may not make them 'good' by the traditional rubric...but it is certainly going to affect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:47:27-07:00","id":909386,"title":"","content":"So, I've said it before and I will say it again: Exalted is not Roleplaying 101. It's, like, College Senior Dissertation Roleplaying. It's rules-heavy and thematically DENSE. Is Achilles a &quot;good guy&quot; the way a children's character like He-Man or Batman is? Is Gilgamesh? I could go on a whole rant about sun heroes in myth and narrative, but the short answer is, <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;The Solar Exalted are heroes who embody human excellence and achievement. They must be GRAND and GLORIOUS.&quot;</b> <br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of wonderful answers on this thread, but I feel like the real issue at the heart of the post is that the OP had a vision as Solars as The Avengers (which is a valid way to play them) but the rest of his troupe was feeling more &quot;HBO series.&quot; <br /> <br /> The question to bounce back is, &quot;Can you still have fun playing Solar Jesus in this party of miscreants?&quot; In a group of truly xcellent roleplayers, you definitely can, ASSUMING the rest of the group does indeed go along with your desire to &quot;fix&quot; them. If they don't, you'll likely get frustrated and feel impotent, as there is very little less enjoyable than being the boyscout everyone mocks. At this point, you can either have THEM influence YOU to become more morally flexible, or you'll want to just reroll anyway. Assuming excellent group alchemy, you'll all play off each other and the characters will grow as people and everyone will have fun times.<br /> <br /> Clearly the majority of the OP's group wants grittier, feet-of-clay heroes, or outright scoundrels who are just excellent at being scoundrels. Only stick with a morally upright character if you're confident you can have fun and be effective playing him in such a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:22:28-07:00","id":909512,"title":"","content":"A Solar is perfectly permitted to be as virtuous and great a leader as King Arthur, fighting to institute a just rule and defending his people while pushing back against vicious invaders. <a href=\"https://hefenfelth.wordpress.com/2009/01/10/the-red-ravagers/\" target=\"_blank\">There is an unavoidable ambiguity in such a statement, however.</a><br /> <br /> (OTOH, that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gwrgi_Garwlwyd\" target=\"_blank\">Gwrgi Garwlwyd </a>is totally a Lunar.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's worth noting that a lot of characters in some of the pulp and fantasy stories that Exalted draws on are impressive people who are not without their virtues, but they're also not easily mappable to a notion of 'good'. (I'm thinking of Jirel of Joiry and the various protagonists of the Flat Earth stories, especially Azhriaz, for example. Hell, looking at the Three Kingdoms, Cao Cao can be as much a model for a Solar as the three heroes are, and it's not like the three heroes are terribly nice people.) None of this is to say that you can't play a character who is a decent person by modern standards, of course, but 'good guy' is a bit difficult to pin down in a meaningful and simple way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 06-07-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:37:25-07:00","id":909524,"title":"","content":"I think more people are drawn to heroic characters that are ambiguously good than they credit themselves, regardless of what setting they're placed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T15:44:36-07:00","id":909536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909524#post909524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more people are drawn to heroic characters that are ambiguously good than they credit themselves, regardless of what setting they're placed in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thinking of most of the PCs I've played, they're usually people who have aims I'd recognise as good and strongly sympathise with -- but I'm not sure that I'd find spending a long period in their vicinity in RL to be exactly a pleasant experience. (Though it might be morally edifying in a kind of 'by negative example' sense [1].)<br /> <br /> [1] 'If you want to keep your hands clean, don't get involved in Realm politics or found militant revolutionary organisations.' And so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:49:19-07:00","id":909588,"title":"","content":"My take has generally been that Solars are <i>heroes,</i> and to me the litmus test is that some community or class of people somewhere, if they could hypothetically see the Solar's life and deeds, should be looking at your character and saying &quot;she's my hero&quot;. Yes, that is incredibly subjective, because the things they admire just have to at least more than cancel out the things they don't admire. Just like when real-life people decide who to look up to.<br /> <br /> So a pirate-Solar might be admired by the people the West because he goes after the ships of the oppressive Realm, or he might be admired by other pirates because he is the best at pirate, and either group might ignore otherwise deplorable behaviors if a) they're visited on someone else and therefore easier to ignore and/or b) his greatness is so great that everyone can politely look the other way when he does bad stuff. And again, all the subjectivity there is a feature, not a bug. If you are a great figure but such a psychopath that even &quot;your own people&quot; (the ones who think you great) can't collectively, and hypothetically, look past it, to my mind you're an <i>excellent</i> candidate for Abyssal or Infernal Exaltation, but not a Solar one. Probably not a Celestial one in general. <br /> <br /> From my perspective Solars who don't meet this standard have either fallen off the path or are on their way to it, with all the drama that implies.<br /> <br /> I think this is at least <i>consistent </i>with how Solars have been presented in the game line, even if it's not the only way to play it. Can anyone think of a Solar who doesn't meet this standard? Even the oft-touted &quot;Evil Solar&quot; Havesh the Vanisher works, from the perspective of an oppressed pariah caste who think the fear he incites and death he brings to the oppressor castes is more than worth the immoral &quot;fringe benefits&quot; he gets along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:59:45-07:00","id":909599,"title":"","content":"I suppose I can grant that most stories that present protagonists of character that is varying degrees of dubious don't posit that their status as protagonists was something bestowed upon them by some kind of well-intentioned authority.<br /> <br /> \u200bIncidentally, I find the occasionally slipped in reference to the idea of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted as being, or at least heavily favouring, unambiguously terrible people to be odd.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-07-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:09:01-07:00","id":909606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909599#post909599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I can grant that most stories that present protagonists of character that is varying degrees of dubious don't posit that their status as protagonists was something bestowed upon them by some kind of well-intentioned authority.<br /> <br /> \u200bIncidentally, I find the occasionally slipped in reference to the idea of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted as being, or at least heavily favouring, unambiguously terrible people to be odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed that there was nothing in the setting that was ALL bad save a handful of demons and alot of Fair Folk and even then it might be more accurate to say 'alien' than bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:25:31-07:00","id":909620,"title":"","content":"Well guess stuffs worth thinking about for 3e:<br /> -The Infernal preview did say that they are going to be the &quot;Solar at their worst...cursed-eaten tyrants and madmen of the twilight of the first age&quot;. So take it as you will.<br /> -The Abyssal preview seems to focus on vengeance, since they are the solars who were caste down by the knives of the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:33:31-07:00","id":909628,"title":"","content":"I suppose I might be reading such statements as positing a universal when they're doing no such thing. I mean, if I can posit that there are Solars who would be dubious but almost never outright terrible, I can probably also see Abyssals and Infernals as being able to include such people where Solars would not, while also not being limited to or defined by such characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the rest... I would be comfortable calling many Deathlords evil in who they are and what they do (while also being restrained enough that it's possible to conduct diplomatic relations with them, and charismatic enough to beguile their deathknights through methods other than outright lies).<br /> <br /> With Fair Folk... yes, I'd mostly fall back on them being weird. Even the worst of them coming across like the Gentleman with the Thistle-Down Hair.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:37:31-07:00","id":909631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909588#post909588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a pirate-Solar might be admired by the people the West because he goes after the ships of the oppressive Realm, or he might be admired by other pirates because he is the best at pirate, and either group might ignore otherwise deplorable behaviors if a) they're visited on someone else and therefore easier to ignore</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally, when someone visits otherwise-deplorable behaviors on someone one deplores, one doesn't ignore those behaviors, one <i>lauds</i> them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:37:37-07:00","id":909632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909599#post909599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIncidentally, I find the occasionally slipped in reference to the idea of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted as being, or at least heavily favouring, unambiguously terrible people to be odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they have to be unambiguously terrible any more than Solars have to be unambiguosuly good, but in the context of my earlier post the mechanisms of those Exaltations <i>do</i> have volition, and <i>are</i> going to Exalt people who they think will further their goals, and their goals <i>are</i> the end of the world (either entirely or at least as we know it). So just like Solars will at least have the potential to do great things, Abyssals and Infernals will at least have the potential to do awful, awful things. Your best bet is someone who is <i>already </i>awful, even by the standards of their own &quot;peer group&quot;; the pirate who is so rapacious or the lawman so brutal or the scholar so incautious that even other pirates or lawmen or scholars are like &quot;whoa, dude, ease up&quot;. But sometimes it's enough to have a deep-seated anger or anguish or shame that, at least to the Exalting volition, will eventually lead a talented and capable person to the dark side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909631#post909631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally, when someone visits otherwise-deplorable behaviors on someone one deplores, one doesn't ignore those behaviors, one <i>lauds</i> them.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, though I think that reinforces my overall point more than anything. That's basically the logic behind my Havesh example. Though being indiscriminate means the positive &quot;those assholes had it coming&quot; points turn into doubly-negative points, hero-wise. A rabid animal isn't a hero even if he happens to be in your enemy's camp at the moment; he comes near <i>your</i> camp and he's still a rabid animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-07-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:04:13-07:00","id":909655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909632#post909632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their goals <i>are</i> the end of the world</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell... possibly. We'll see how that all plays out.<br /> <br /> I think it might raise the question of what the actual mechanism of ending the world might be, and if somebody who would be horrifically evil would necessarily be competent at enacting the precise methods. Even if it was just something as simple as &quot;kill everybody&quot;, that's the kind of thing that is simple in principle but can be kind of complicated in practice.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt makes me think of how in Mass Effect, they had the idea that the Reaper occupation of Earth was killing close to two million people per day, which is a lot, but still a rate that would take ten years to wipe out the population.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:10:16-07:00","id":909660,"title":"","content":"For the infernals...it's the reclamation and this time at least the Yozis actually have a plan in the preview. A very amusing plan in the grand scheme of things, they are using the first generation of Infernals to gain powers/collect powers, essentially the more the Green Sun Princes grow in power, the more power they get (So even your renegade green sun prince and bleeding heart ends up helping the Yozis), while the loyalists get showered with gifts and the powers of Hell, they plan to make a second generation of Infernal, who are stronger and more powerful than the first. A detail that they currently hide from the first generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:15:28-07:00","id":909667,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> There's evil and there's evil. Given their purview and purpose, it's hard to argue the vast majority of Abyssals and Infernals find it easy to be life-affirming heroes. I'd I'd say it's <b>boring</b> to want them to just be another flavor of Solar with black or green explosions instead of golden ones. They are, if heroes, vastly different sorts of heroes.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are heroes of brutal and nihilistic expedience -- The Punisher is an Abyssal. <br /> <br /> Infernals are heroes of twisted and eldritch causes -- Elric of Melnibone is an Infernal.<br /> <br /> Then you can also have Infernals or Abyssals who reject their calling and seek to become pure, life-affirming heroes again. These are redemptive heroes. Darth Vader or Miltion's Lucifer. <br /> <br /> For my part, I tend to have the vast majority of Abyssal Exalted be the horrible necromantic reapers of flesh they're mostly described as being. That makes the small divergent faction (which will likely include a PC or two) compelling. <br /> <br /> Every last Green Sun Prince, meanwhile, is one of the fifty most horrible humans alive in Creation. At best, you have high-functioning sociopaths who can be reasoned with so long as your interests and theirs align and you plan to betray them before they betray you. If your Infernal Exalted don't feel like Apostles or the God-Hand from Berserk, they are very little like my Infernal Exalted. The Yozis, you'll recall, have only 50 Essences with which to turn Creation into Hell. They would be super selective about their recruiting. <br /> <br /> That said, if I had a player who absotively <b>had</b> to play a Green Sun Prince, I would work with him to make the character some sort of Noble Demon or Magnificent Bastard. An anti-villain who could function in my generally quite heroic party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:15:41-07:00","id":909668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909655#post909655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might raise the question of what the actual mechanism of ending the world might be, and if somebody who would be horrifically evil would necessarily be competent at enacting the precise methods. Even if it was just something as simple as &quot;kill everybody&quot;, that's the kind of thing that is simple in principle but can be kind of complicated in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they don't (usually) Exalt raving lunatics, they Exalt talented capable people who have reason to want to see the world burn. Or people they can <i>make</i> capable and talented; there is a persistent Abyssal theme of taking young or inexperienced people with emotional scars and teaching them how to be badasses while cultivating their nihilism. Sometimes it works (Son of Crows, Shoat of the Mire), sometimes it doesn't (Secret).<br /> <br /> Of course, they're also crazy undying-or-imprisoned god-monsters from before the birth of the world, so sometimes they pick someone batshit. Made sense at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:37:31-07:00","id":909688,"title":"","content":"I'll put my views simply: Can Solars be the good guys? Absolutely! Must they be the good guys? Absolutely not! <br /> <br /> To elaborate, I'll use the circle I created for my rewritten version of Wu-Jian. The most straightforwardly heroic are the Dawn and Zenith, whose goals are to unite the gangs of the slums, thereby creating what will amount to a police force, and to promote trade and commerce between the islands and the West, reducing their need for the Blessed Isle and easing the tensions between the city folk and the other islanders. The Twilight just wants the Realm out before their greed destroys Wu-Jian's economy. The Eclipse is an actress and an infiltration expert, and the Night is a sort of Bronze Age Batwoman. Since there's no real law in the slums, she works on her own principles, and will kill when needed. For an example of morality we'd consider &quot;off&quot; she ruined the drug dealer whose product killed her mother. Not because he sold her drugs, but because he'd sold her tainted drugs. She hates that people need drugs to get by, but she's a slum kid; she understands the need. Basically, if you harm or cheat the gutter folk, she's sudden death. Offer an honest good or service, she has no trouble with you. You're a whore? Fine. Rob a client? Not fine. Hire a whore? Fine. Stiff one? Not fine. The one group she absolutely will come crashing down on every time? Slavers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:41:54-07:00","id":909692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909668#post909668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">want to see the world burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI want to be clear that I'm focusing on this turn of phrase specifically rather than you or any greater point you might be making when I<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://gif-finder.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/Liz-Lemon-Eye-Roll.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm sorry just... urrggh, I hate that phrase. What does it even mean!<br /> <br /> It doesn't even make sense in its original pop cultural context. Oh yeah, Alfred, I'm sure that bandit leader was intercepting shipments of bribes and tributes to tribal leaders without trying to liquidate them for profit was motivated by sport rather than any kind of opposition to either British imperialist or military dictatorship agendas.<br /> <br /> Urrggh, I've got to stop right there, otherwise I will rant endlessly about how disturbing I've always found a scene in which Alfred not only openly admits involvement with regimes in Burma of all places, but tries to use such to teach somebody a lesson predicated on something other than not involving oneself in oppressive regimes.<br /> <br /> (Not even getting into stuff about how he may be an actual war criminal)<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's late, and I think I have no energy for arguing points about what the purpose and nature of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted is, so maybe I'll try picking up tomorrow (preferably in a new thread).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-07-2016, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:43:58-07:00","id":909693,"title":"","content":"Ugh. I haaaaaaate this slippery slope trope of &quot;If they're evil, they must be wackypants crazy!&quot; No. <br /> <br /> Just because you've played with doofuses who think &quot;Evil PCs&quot; automatically means &quot;Hop aboard the Arsonmurderape Train! Woowooooo!&quot; doesn't mean there aren't plenty of compelling, intelligent beings available for play. <br /> <br /> A list of non-wacky evil characters: Tony Soprano, Tywin Lannister, Gustavo Fring, Doctor Doom, Sauron, Emperor Palpatine, Kingpin, Hannibal Lecter, Hans Landa, Nosferatu Zod, Femto/Griffith, Maleficent (the animated one), The Other Mother, Randall Flagg, Nurse Ratched, Jadis the White Witch, Dolores Umbridge, Catherine Tramell. <br /> <br /> Seriously, the idea that all or even most villainous PCs need to be Your Cousin Biff Who Thinks Roleplaying is His Revenge Fantasy makes ol' Foxy wanna drop the Macho Elbow on some fools. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.stillrealtous.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/machoman12.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:48:40-07:00","id":909697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909693#post909693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. I haaaaaaate this slippery slope trope of &quot;If they're evil, they must be wackypants crazy!&quot; No.<br /> <br /> Just because you've played with doofuses who think &quot;Evil PCs&quot; automatically means &quot;Hop aboard the Arsonmurderape Train! Woowooooo!&quot; doesn't mean there aren't plenty of compelling, intelligent beings available for play.<br /> <br /> A list of non-wacky evil characters: Tony Soprano, Tywin Lannister, Gustavo Fring, Doctor Doom, Sauron, Emperor Palpatine, Kingpin, Hannibal Lecter, Hans Landa, Nosferatu Zod, Femto/Griffith, Maleficent (the animated one), The Other Mother, Randall Flagg, Nurse Ratched, Jadis the White Witch, Dolores Umbridge, Catherine Tramell.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the idea that all or even most villainous PCs need to be Your Cousin Biff Who Thinks Roleplaying is His Revenge Fantasy makes ol' Foxy wanna drop the Macho Elbow on some fools.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.stillrealtous.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/machoman12.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First off, fantastic list! <br /> <br /> Second, stealing the shit out of that gif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:15:33-07:00","id":909718,"title":"","content":"Not saying that this needs to apply to Exalted, but... The classical concept of the hero is 'paragon of his society's virtues'. That can make a lot of classical heroes seem ... pretty not-moral. Achilles was a killer and a rapist, with a major case of the rages, but he's considered a hero by the ancient greeks because he was an awesome fighter who swayed the course of a ten year war, and when motivated by the loss of someone he loved, tore down an army. Odysseus was a philanderer with a cruel streak, but his cunning won a war, and his journey home threw him into conflict with sorcery, monsters, and gods which he prevailed against through an application of that same intellect. A lot of the things we see as 'evil' in these heroes are simply not important to the greek culture because their values are different from ours. They didn't consider women to be... well, people. They saw martial skill and loyalty as important, intellect doubly so. The other things didn't factor so much for them as a simple matter of values dissonance. <br /> <br /> When it comes to Solars, I'd say in some sense they should reflect that. Creation is a big place, there's room for a broad range of cultures, each of whom have their own values, their own perspectives, and their own dissonance. Some Immaculate-raised son of a Great House is going to have vastly different opinions about what 'good' or 'virtue' means, as compared to the various threshold societies.<br /> <br /> Again, not universally applicable here, but worth considering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:26:48-07:00","id":909729,"title":"","content":"I agree, and it's also why I think it would be very difficult, if Solars had to be good, for STs and players to decide whether they are good or not. I mean, what if they make a character that seems okay and are then a bad person during the game, does their exaltation fall off? Are players going to write up characters who want vengeance for their dead sifu, and then the ST says &quot;no, you're not good&quot;? It doesn't really work.<br /> <br /> Solars are supposed, as people have said, to emulate mythic heroes, and a lot of mythic heroes weren't that great by modern standards (don't ever make fun of their baldness!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every last Green Sun Prince, meanwhile, is one of the fifty most horrible humans alive in Creation. At best, you have high-functioning sociopaths who can be reasoned with so long as your interests and theirs align and you plan to betray them before they betray you. If your Infernal Exalted don't feel like Apostles or the God-Hand from Berserk, they are very little like my Infernal Exalted. The Yozis, you'll recall, have only 50 Essences with which to turn Creation into Hell. They would be super selective about their recruiting. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but those aren't the sort of people they would select, because they're too untrustworthy. They're likely to betray the Yozis. The Yozis after all, are not simply &quot;evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> What I'd expect them to do with their selection is to choose people loyal to the Yozis. For example, the signature Defiler was a member of a Yozi cultist, while the signature Malefactor hated the Unconquered Sun (which makes sense, being a dune person).<br /> <br /> They want committed fanatics, not arsonmurderrapists.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:27:41-07:00","id":909731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909693#post909693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh. I haaaaaaate this slippery slope trope of &quot;If they're evil, they must be wackypants crazy!&quot; No.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're saying, but I'm unsure of why. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:33:20-07:00","id":909737,"title":"","content":"I am suddenly remembering certain positions that have been held regarding Infernal Exalted in the past, and am unsure that I want to get into that discussion after all...<br /> <br /> Other than maybe to express the idea that the position of &quot;the Green Sun Princes are the worst of what is human&quot; is singular enough that it doesn't really make for firm grounds for a discussion, even regarding how they were written before, and certainly not for how they might be written anew several years from now. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:01:46-07:00","id":909765,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one that liked that Yozi, Deathlords &amp; Incarna used to be personified to the degree that they could make blunders? I find it entirely possible that one these entities would misjudge a candidate or would simply only be able to hedge their bets as to the likely outcome, oh sure this guy is a real jerk who wants to destroy the world but how sure can the Deathlords ever be that being given a plausible means to do it wouldn't result in him/her stopping to reconsider? By that same token the US is sure that this person can be a great Solar but he cannot be undoubtedly sure that this person won't become 'great' in the Attila the Hun way (from a Roman perspective).<br /> For me personally I tend to focus more on the PCs personality and skills alot more when considering any real criteria, people without drive or ability? They shouldn't be a Solar. No indomitable drive to survive? You should not be a Lunar. You aren't fond of weaponizing super-villain tropes or swivel chairs in ominous lairs? You should not be an Infernal. Don't like fratricide? You shouldn't be a DB, etc.<br /> YMMV on how strictly your players should follow those rules but exceptions to this should have an equally exceptional reason (and I mean exceptional even by the already exceptional nature of an Exalt) why they didnt just exalt as something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:16:04-07:00","id":909775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909692#post909692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI want to be clear that I'm focusing on this turn of phrase specifically rather than you or any greater point you might be making when I<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://gif-finder.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/Liz-Lemon-Eye-Roll.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm sorry just... urrggh, I hate that phrase. What does it even mean!<br /> <br /> It doesn't even make sense in its original pop cultural context. Oh yeah, Alfred, I'm sure that bandit leader was intercepting shipments of bribes and tributes to tribal leaders without trying to liquidate them for profit was motivated by sport rather than any kind of opposition to either British imperialist or military dictatorship agendas.<br /> <br /> Urrggh, I've got to stop right there, otherwise I will rant endlessly about how disturbing I've always found a scene in which Alfred not only openly admits involvement with regimes in Burma of all places, but tries to use such to teach somebody a lesson predicated on something other than not involving oneself in oppressive regimes.<br /> <br /> (Not even getting into stuff about how he may be an actual war criminal)<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's late, and I think I have no energy for arguing points about what the purpose and nature of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted is, so maybe I'll try picking up tomorrow (preferably in a new thread).</div> </div> </div> </div>That phrase with that general meaning is older than The Dark Knight; Google ngrams gave at least one generally-the-same reference from 1813 and an even closer one from 1916, and that was just a quick skim. Heck, I'm pretty sure it showed up more than once in the OWOD (esp. Mage, maybe re: Nephandi?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-07-2016, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:45:17-07:00","id":909792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909737#post909737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am suddenly remembering certain positions that have been held regarding Infernal Exalted in the past, and am unsure that I want to get into that discussion after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not trying to start that old shootin' war up again. Infernals can be played however you want them played at your table. I'm just talking about how <b>I</b> run them in <b>my </b>game. Which is as a cavalcade of very diverse horrors. I think that's the most compelling thing to do with them anyhow. There's certainly space within the canon for anti-heroic and heroic GSPs. I'm just not interested in any of that bollocks, thank you very much. <br /> <br /> My rant about &quot;evil =/= wackypants rapemurder&quot; was meant to be an agreement with something <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar456_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"456\" data-vbnamecard=\"456\">Blackwell</a> said, not a refutation of anything you said. <br /> <br /> And of course not every Infernal is untrustworthy to the Yozis themselves. Some are quite loyal. Others less so. What they share in common is a vision of their own dominion over a world brought low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:49:40-07:00","id":909793,"title":"","content":"This came up in an exploration of the Zenith caste, but I think it applies to Exalts as a whole. Basically many a Zenith's message boils down to &quot;do the right thing and be righteous.&quot; Problem is Exalts are still human and it's not like they're given a device that lets them know if they're about to do something wrong. So an Exalt will do what they think is right, but that in no way means that will be moral, right, just, or not horrifyingly evil acts.<br /> <br /> For example there's a character mentioned in the history of &quot;Wiseman's Fear&quot; who apparently did more to advance medicine than anyone else in the history of the setting. Of course he did this by doing such things as dissecting people alive, peeling off layers of the body to see how they work, and all kind of other horrible and monstrous things, but there's a note in his journal that implies he did all of this because he felt that these actions were for a greater good. (He's only come up once and I'm still reading no spoilers if anything else comes up on him please.) Or there's a character in the Stormlight Archives series. Due to a number of events apparently the guy has a plan to save the world (He's pretty sure anyway he's still translating the plan and he wasn't all there when he came up with it.) This plan involves basically the assassination of a large amount of the settings world leaders in very specific methods; this plan involves starting wars; this plan involves a room full of people of all ages having their blood slowly drained out of their bodies, because sometimes a person will give part of a prophecy or something in their dying moments. All of this he feels is justified because it will save the world. That's part of the conflict in Exalted. When you have the power to change the world, how do you exercise it, and should you exercise it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T20:52:13-07:00","id":909797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909692#post909692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI want to be clear that I'm focusing on this turn of phrase specifically rather than you or any greater point you might be making when I<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://gif-finder.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/02/Liz-Lemon-Eye-Roll.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm sorry just... urrggh, I hate that phrase. What does it even mean!<br /> <br /> It doesn't even make sense in its original pop cultural context. Oh yeah, Alfred, I'm sure that bandit leader was intercepting shipments of bribes and tributes to tribal leaders without trying to liquidate them for profit was motivated by sport rather than any kind of opposition to either British imperialist or military dictatorship agendas.<br /> <br /> Urrggh, I've got to stop right there, otherwise I will rant endlessly about how disturbing I've always found a scene in which Alfred not only openly admits involvement with regimes in Burma of all places, but tries to use such to teach somebody a lesson predicated on something other than not involving oneself in oppressive regimes.<br /> <br /> (Not even getting into stuff about how he may be an actual war criminal)<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's late, and I think I have no energy for arguing points about what the purpose and nature of Abyssal and Infernal Exalted is, so maybe I'll try picking up tomorrow (preferably in a new thread).</div> </div> </div> </div>*The Joker* just wants the world to burn.<br /> <br /> The point of the story about the bandit is not necessarily to give an example of someone who 'just wants the world to burn&quot; but to shake Bruce into seeing other people can have dramatically different motives than would seem obvious; Alfred and his company had been baffled by that man because they thought he was a bandit motivated by profit *and he wasn't*.<br /> <br /> (Much like The Joker wasn't motivated by profit)<br /> <br /> <br /> (And, to be fair, the man was presumably motivated by a desire to see the British Imperial Presence in Burma burn, i.e. he just wanted them to fail and die)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:10:25-07:00","id":909810,"title":"","content":"I feel like &quot;watch the world burn&quot; was an apt description for that particular iteration of the Joker or other nihilistic villains. It's definitely not the only motivation horrible enough to get you an Infernal Exaltation in my playbook. Doctor Doom doesn't want to watch the world burn, but he's an Infernal if ever one existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:34:04-07:00","id":909820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, noble peepsicles of assorted flavours. After searching deep within myself, and on this fine forum, I've been unable to find an answer to this simplest of questions. Are Solars the good guys?<br /> <br /> I've played exactly one session of Exalted, although I'm more familiar with the setting and mechanics, because A: I'm the only player in my group able to read the goddamn book apparently, and B: Our ST is a giant Exalted fanboy. I created a character in the expectation of !Heroic Endeavour Style! and !Innocent Saving Prana!, but after our first session, I'm finding that my party are... not the good guys. Maybe that's just the people I'm playing with, but we've got one devious snake-tongued trust-betraying sidereal-in-solar's-clothing, one Lawful Evil Bureaucrat, one straight-up rape-and-murder pirate and one ex-mercenary bent on killing every dishonourable employer he's ever had (does this count as good?). In the middle of this party, I'm playing... basically Jesus. Am I doing it wrong? Are they doing it wrong? Are we -supposed- to be actual Anathema, or is there simply something I'm missing?<br /> <br /> I really need help with this problem before Sunday if possible, because I like my character, but if evil Solars are totally legitimate, i'm going to have to roll up a new character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Evil&quot; Solars are legitimate. No faction of Exalted are &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; by definition. Free will is a central component of Exaltation, so how people chose to use their power varies mightely. The Unconquered Sun's will that drives Exaltation (whether he's consciously guiding it or not) obviously leans away from Exalting someone who wants all of Creation to be destroyed - but his definition of &quot;heroism&quot; beyond that can definitely have a Bronze Age selfish-but-awesome flavor to it, or ends justify the means hard-man-of-hard-decisions etc etc (he's ineffable like that). Work out with your Storyteller and the other players what type of campaign they want to run and proceed accordingly.<br /> <br /> If another player is actually intending to have his character commit rapes, that is definitely something I would personally look askance at, but not something that inherently contradicts canon. Just good taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T00:47:30-07:00","id":909907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909820#post909820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Evil&quot; Solars are legitimate. No faction of Exalted are &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot; by definition. Free will is a central component of Exaltation, so how people chose to use their power varies mightely. The Unconquered Sun's will that drives Exaltation (whether he's consciously guiding it or not) obviously leans away from Exalting someone who wants all of Creation to be destroyed - but his definition of &quot;heroism&quot; beyond that can definitely have a Bronze Age selfish-but-awesome flavor to it, or ends justify the means hard-man-of-hard-decisions etc etc (he's ineffable like that). Work out with your Storyteller and the other players what type of campaign they want to run and proceed accordingly.<br /> <br /> If another player is actually intending to have his character commit rapes, that is definitely something I would personally look askance at, but not something that inherently contradicts canon. Just good taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Just&quot; good taste; good taste &gt; canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T01:26:50-07:00","id":909915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909907#post909907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Just&amp;quot; good taste; good taste &gt; canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you, it's not something I'd allow at my own table, but for &quot;this isn't what we're here to play&quot; and &quot;what the fuck is wrong with you?!&quot; reasons, not &quot;this is impossible for this character type to do in-setting&quot; reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T01:36:17-07:00","id":909919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909718#post909718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying that this needs to apply to Exalted, but... The classical concept of the hero is 'paragon of his society's virtues'. That can make a lot of classical heroes seem ... pretty not-moral. Achilles was a killer and a rapist, with a major case of the rages, but he's considered a hero by the ancient greeks because he was an awesome fighter who swayed the course of a ten year war, and when motivated by the loss of someone he loved, tore down an army. Odysseus was a philanderer with a cruel streak, but his cunning won a war, and his journey home threw him into conflict with sorcery, monsters, and gods which he prevailed against through an application of that same intellect. A lot of the things we see as 'evil' in these heroes are simply not important to the greek culture because their values are different from ours. They didn't consider women to be... well, people. They saw martial skill and loyalty as important, intellect doubly so. The other things didn't factor so much for them as a simple matter of values dissonance.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Solars, I'd say in some sense they should reflect that. Creation is a big place, there's room for a broad range of cultures, each of whom have their own values, their own perspectives, and their own dissonance. Some Immaculate-raised son of a Great House is going to have vastly different opinions about what 'good' or 'virtue' means, as compared to the various threshold societies.<br /> <br /> Again, not universally applicable here, but worth considering.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wanted to refer to this one specifically, because the last game I ran was Fate, set in the mythical mediterranean. They were all flawed heroes, as the greek heroes are, but they were all unequivocally -heroes-. The game ended a bit bleakly, because they had been unknowingly unsealing the binds that kept Thanatos (represented here as an angry child throwing all his toys out of the pram) and one of the heroes sided with him for the promise of a better world once the Olympian gods had been purged. The unbinding was completed by one member of the party at the same time that the gods were alerted to the whole scheme, Thanatos killed everyone except the loyal PC, and then the PC got a suitably eternal punishment for trying to destroy the world.<br /> <br /> I would class every single member of that party as a hero, for all their faults. Not necessarily by our standards, but by the definition of &quot;would someone have written their tales on papyrus?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Top up question - I'm personally unhappy with the idea of using the powers of a solar to instill intimacies in other PCs, but is that a legitimate thing to do in most people's opinions? I think it probably depends entirely on the group, and I need to ask mine before I go all Fulminating Word on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 06-08-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T02:36:17-07:00","id":909936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909919#post909919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Top up question - I'm personally unhappy with the idea of using the powers of a solar to instill intimacies in other PCs, but is that a legitimate thing to do in most people's opinions. I think it probably depends entirely on the group, and I need to ask mine before I go all Fulminating Word on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is <i>technically</i> legitimate, but it is a kin to a Red Rule thing.<br /> <br /> Player's tend to object to others &quot;taking control&quot; of their characters out side of &quot;let us role play with this idea&quot; situations.<br /> <br /> Definitely get agreement before trying to work it into the script.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T03:30:54-07:00","id":909953,"title":"","content":"I also find that with a lot (but not all) of the players, instilling intimacies doesn't work that well, because they just don't role-play them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T03:48:32-07:00","id":909961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909953#post909953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also find that with a lot (but not all) of the players, instilling intimacies doesn't work that well, because they just don't role-play them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that's a separate issue entirely. The only reason I didn't have my Solar punch the devious Sidereal-wannabe in his face is because my character is defined by his belief in compassion and mercy in all things. Stupid &quot;morals&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T06:49:33-07:00","id":910032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909919#post909919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Top up question - I'm personally unhappy with the idea of using the powers of a solar to instill intimacies in other PCs, but is that a legitimate thing to do in most people's opinions? I think it probably depends entirely on the group, and I need to ask mine before I go all Fulminating Word on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a legitimate use of powers, and here's why. The social influence system models all human interaction. If you and your fellow gaming nerds are trying to decide to order pizza or chinese for dinner, and you say &quot;I had pizza last night. Can we skip it this week? We can do pizza next week.&quot; then you just engaged in social influence. You are bargaining with them, or instilling an Intimacy of sympathy like &quot;I don't like eating pizza two nights in a row, either.&quot; There's nothing malicious or coercive in it.<br /> <br /> However, players often perceive ANY actions upon their character sheet as coercive, and particularly inexperienced roleplayers react defensively and negatively to such things. That situation is, again, something that should be addressed at an OC level with the group at large. I think many groups will knee jerk their way to &quot;no social influence on fellow PCs,&quot; and that might work for them. But, they have just removed the only guide the system has for resolving disputes between PCs, which means OC social dynamics are more likely to influence the game.<br /> <br /> At my table, I took pains to explain how the social influence system worked, and what it modeled. My players are mostly new, but they are mature people, and they get along. They have done a fantastic job playing their characters well the few times they used social influence on each other. It helps that I made them all build up Intimacies of trust and loyalty to each other as a requisite for their concepts. I can then say &quot;Dexanus Ilessa is telling you to put the sword away and trust her. She has successfully convinced you that she knows what's going on. What do you do?&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if your group agrees to interact with the system for what it is, rather than as a vector of attack, and your ST actively narrates the outcomes of the rolls such that they prompt the players to contextualize the rolls, it can work rather well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  Moar typos! 06-08-2016, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:10:53-07:00","id":910051,"title":"","content":"I think that for the vast majority of players, if you end up in a situation where they're saying &quot;I want my character to do X&quot; and another player across the table from them say &quot;no, I'm gonna roll dice and make you do Y instead&quot;, they're going to see that as an attack. The terminology isn't important and isn't going to change how players feel about it.<br /> <br /> Players are at the table because they want to play a specific character, who acts in a specific way. To a certain extent, saying &quot;no, it's not magical compulsion, it's what your character actually wants&quot; makes it <i>even worse</i>, because you're changing their basic character concept by doing it (rather than just making one attack they can later recover from -- even if they later lose the intimacy or stop doing what you said, they can't change the fact that you defined their character as someone who would sometimes think or act that way.)<br /> <br /> <i>Sometimes</i> you might be able to sell them on a change that makes the character more interesting; but sometimes, changing their character's intimacies will result in something they have no interesting playing, and that is absolutely something everyone at the table has to respect. If I was an ST and a player insisted on trying to instill an intimacy in another PC that that other player clearly wasn't comfortable with, I'd probably boot them, because you just do not do that. The game requires that everybody be on the same page, which means that (unless you've agreed in advance that this will be a PVP-ish game), if you're making a social attack on another PC that their player doesn't want, you are at least <i>very close</i> to the point where the entire game collapses under mutually incompatible expectations.<br /> <br /> And because of that, I am extremely leery of arguments that go along the lines of &quot;you just have to accept the social system as it is and not get all uptight about it&quot;, because the underlying subtext is &quot;if you're not a wuss, you'll play out this scene even though you obviously really don't want to&quot;, and that is grade-A nuclear-class bullshit.<br /> <br /> Now, 3e's social system tries to reduce this a bit by giving players a way to map out their character and making it really really hard to make a character do something that wasn't at least notionally on their initial map of what the character is like. But ultimately, everyone at the table should be trying to ensure that everyone else has fun; if it's clear that what you're doing isn't fun for the other players, and you're still pushing it, you're ruining the game for every else and don't belong there. And this means, to me, that <i>most of the time</i> the social system is not going to be used between PCs unless it's to do trivial things or things both players are obviously happy with.<br /> <br /> (Keeping in mind that another thing the 3e social system does is provide places where you can use social &quot;support&quot; roles on other players to eg. play a therapist who removes unwanted intimacies or adds ones they want; it's not like forcing people to do things is the only use for it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-08-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:32:30-07:00","id":910068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909797#post909797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And, to be fair, the man was presumably motivated by a desire to see the British Imperial Presence in Burma burn, i.e. he just wanted them to fail and die)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not fair at all.<br /> <br /> &quot;He wanted to hurt the British Imperial Presence in Burma specifically&quot; (because they're doing awful shit in general / because he wants to free his nation / because he hates them for killing his spouse or child or parent or dog, etc) is very very different from &quot;he wanted to make everyone in the entire world suffer for lolz because he was irrational and evil.&quot; And more importantly, by automatically assuming that it's the latter, Alfred is implicitly whitewashing both the government of Burma and his own involvement with it.<br /> <br /> He can say &quot;well, that man was just twisted and sick and evil and needed to be put down&quot; without looking at the situation in more depth, which is convenient for him because if he <i>did</i> look at it in any more depth, it's very likely that the guy actually had some sort of motivation or goal which might have made Alfred question what the hell he was doing working for the Burmese government.<br /> <br /> (Of course, this is an underlying theme when it comes to Batman and vigilante comics in general. Some versions, like TAS, managed to avoid this trap, but when Batman is written badly, it doesn't let you look at the underlying causes of crime; it can't even let you suspect that the villains <i>might</i> have a reason to do what they do. For Batman's shtick of dealing with crime by running around punching people in the face to make sense as the best way a <i>fucking billionare</i> could deal with crime, you have to assume that most criminals are soulless monsters who just want to hurt people for the sake of it and will only stop when terrified of someone bigger and darker and more bat-like than themselves.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:48:01-07:00","id":910076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910068#post910068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Of course, this is an underlying theme when it comes to Batman and vigilante comics in general. Some versions, like TAS, managed to avoid this trap, but when Batman is written badly, it doesn't let you look at the underlying causes of crime; it can't even let you suspect that the villains <i>might</i> have a reason to do what they do. For Batman's shtick of dealing with crime by running around punching people in the face to make sense as the best way a <i>fucking billionare</i> could deal with crime, you have to assume that most criminals are soulless monsters who just want to hurt people for the sake of it and will only stop when terrified of someone bigger and darker and more bat-like than themselves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, as is occasionally implied, the city itself is in some fashion malevolent or cursed, with evil being impossible to fully defeat whether you put on a suit and punch criminals or fund charities and police work. Given the problematic implications of most alternatives, I've found this, surprisingly, the most elegant way to handle the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:53:19-07:00","id":910080,"title":"","content":"... Darn, I'm going to have to resist the impulse to make this a conversation about the Batman animated series...<br /> <br /> \u200bFor a slightly more relevant tangent, I generally have difficulty finding credibility in characters who want to destroy the world just because, but think there might be some potential in characters who adhere to equivalents to actual philosophies that view the morality or happiness of human existence to be a dubious subject, who now have the power to see such ideas through.<br /> <br /> Even some things like an Abyssal antinatalist; somebody who wants the creation of new life to cease because it cannot consent to its own creation, making birth an inherently coercive act.<br /> <br /> Although... the existence of reincarnating souls might add an interesting dimension to that question; could a soul have agency sufficient to view it bestowing itself upon a neonate as an indication of it giving consent to its own life? For the purposes of this digression, I would think of that as an ambiguous question even inside the setting.<br /> <br /> Although mostly, I think Abyssals should not be about killing the world so much as they are there to preside and give Law over a world that is already dying. I think that ties them into the purpose of the returning Solars and contrasts them in a more interesting way, and is a better representation of some of the gothic imagery that Abyssals are built out of.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-08-2016, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T07:55:51-07:00","id":910083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910080#post910080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Darn, I'm going to have to resist the impulse to make this a conversation about the Batman animated series...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good series, and given that I've now had two questions answered I'm willing to let this topic tumble off the rails and into the pit that leads inevitably to the second page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:14:11-07:00","id":910126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really need help with this problem before Sunday if possible, because I like my character, but if evil Solars are totally legitimate, i'm going to have to roll up a new character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered speaking to the <u>players</u> of the 'evil' PCs and negotiating a way the characters might get along? I say negotiating, because it requires everyone to bend a little (even Jesus). Just speaking about the problem might result in some slightly less evil characters, if the others decide that maybe they were going a bit 'over the top'. And perhaps your group might come up with some fun themes to explore. Two characters (yours and the pirate for example) could be constantly trying to get the ear of others (especially if you have a party leader) to convince them of how violent/peaceful a plan should be carried out. The Devil on one shoulder, the Angel on the other.<br /> <br /> If you cannot see a way forward, then at least you can save yourself from many aggravating sessions.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Long time lurker","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8781-happy-hermit","name":"Happy Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:35:47-07:00","id":910133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910080#post910080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Darn, I'm going to have to resist the impulse to make this a conversation about the Batman animated series...</div> </div> </div> </div>*Roll to Resist temptation*<br /> <br /> *Critical Fail*<br /> <br /> Bat's is totally a Night Caste Solar.....<br /> Joker is a Fae/Raksha or Green Sun Prince....<br /> Victor Fries is a Dragon-Blood with an Alchemical Suit that Augments him....<br /> Edward Nygma is.... Well A God of Riddles.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry for the Derailment.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:48:25-07:00","id":910142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909029#post909029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly the Devs for this edition deliberately didn't mention or picture any of the cannon solars who were straight-up villains, and have said that each solar carries at least the potential for good in their character. That being said if your ST favors a darker and grittier creation that is his prerogative.</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifically mentions the Bull of the North catapulting livestock fed on human meat into cities as a means of spreading the puppeteer's plague. I'm not sure I would call the Bull of the North a &quot;straight-up&quot; villain, but that's pretty villainous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11872-lessens","name":"lessens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:58:10-07:00","id":910148,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11875_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11875\" data-vbnamecard=\"11875\">Rowanas</a> Have you considered the roll of making your character either function as the balancing force for the group, or the one trying to make them better people? I mean it's been done before and if I recall that's actually part of the reason for Prince Diamond's character in 3rd's iconic circle. Though like Hermit says you could always talk to the other players and see about getting them to tone it down to more antihero levels than full on villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:05:35-07:00","id":910152,"title":"","content":"It's a fun role...as long as people don't think that you are the &quot;Morale Police&quot; trying to take the fun away from them. Personally I don't have a problem with it but I know it's a common mentality of some players to think the person who wants to act like a good person in a group, takes fun away.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T10:22:10-07:00","id":910168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=909321#post909321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My suspicion is that you will find fewer games going with evil Solar PCs than Abyssals, Infernals or even Dragon-Bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like you see more good people than bad people, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:27:37-07:00","id":910212,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910068#post910068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Of course, this is an underlying theme when it comes to Batman and vigilante comics in general. Some versions, like TAS, managed to avoid this trap, but when Batman is written badly, it doesn't let you look at the underlying causes of crime; it can't even let you suspect that the villains <i>might</i> have a reason to do what they do. For Batman's shtick of dealing with crime by running around punching people in the face to make sense as the best way a <i>fucking billionare</i> could deal with crime, you have to assume that most criminals are soulless monsters who just want to hurt people for the sake of it and will only stop when terrified of someone bigger and darker and more bat-like than themselves.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not up on Batman but I think it was implied in the Nolan movies that he funded orphanages (there was an orphanage that Tommy from Third Rock from the Sun came from?) and paid his taxes and whatnot? Which is sort of crime prevent-y.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what more he could actually do, as a billionaire. <br /> <br /> I mean, IRC most criminology shows that the overall crime rates pretty much seem to track the population age distribution (most criminality is age dependent - young men, why it peaked in the 1980s-early 1990s then has fallen off with an increasingly aging population) and otherwise basically random (as far as we know) societal forces that no one has a predictive model for (poverty, recessions, etc - zilch unless they're interacting with some other social motivation factors that aren't modeled).<br /> <br /> So paying your taxes, doing charity that seems to work and at weekends putting on your batsuit and punching some people in the face doesn't seem like that unreasonable a thing to do, given that (assuming we're OK accepting the premise of a man dressing up as a bat and being a vigilante punching criminals in the first place!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:46:34-07:00","id":910222,"title":"","content":"Does the Unconquered Sun still have virtues in 3E?<br /> Do they influence his exaltation choices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:50:51-07:00","id":910225,"title":"","content":"Virtues as a firm mechanical thing are no longer existent in 3E. Motivation is out too. Everything gets modeled with Intimacies, Limit Trigger (what used to be called Virtue Flaw), Limit track, and Willpower.<br /> <br /> That said, he probably has intimacies that do the jobs the Virtues did in previous editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T11:51:12-07:00","id":910226,"title":"","content":"Nobody has Virtues in 3e; they've been dropped in favour of Intimacies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:46:40-07:00","id":910256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lessens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910142#post910142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It specifically mentions the Bull of the North catapulting livestock fed on human meat into cities as a means of spreading the puppeteer's plague. I'm not sure I would call the Bull of the North a &quot;straight-up&quot; villain, but that's pretty villainous.</div> </div> </div> </div>President Harry S. Truman: Straight-up villain, or merely pretty villainous?<br /> <br /> (Also, given that the Bull's forces are sort of a Mongol analogue: <a href=\"http://wwwnc.cdc.gov/eid/article/8/9/01-0536_article\" target=\"_blank\">http://wwwnc.cdc.gov/eid/article/8/9/01-0536_article</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:05:04-07:00","id":910263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910256#post910256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">President Harry S. Truman: Straight-up villain, or merely pretty villainous?<br /> <br /> (Also, given that the Bull's forces are sort of a Mongol analogue: <a href=\"http://wwwnc.cdc.gov/eid/article/8/9/01-0536_article\" target=\"_blank\">http://wwwnc.cdc.gov/eid/article/8/9/01-0536_article</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't wanna derail anything but let's just say I wouldn't be the first person to make an argument like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11872-lessens","name":"lessens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T13:12:22-07:00","id":910271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lessens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910263#post910263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't wanna derail anything but let's just say I wouldn't be the first person to make an argument like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please don't mistake pointing out the existence of a debate for staking out a side in that debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:24:57-07:00","id":910455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910051#post910051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And because of that, I am extremely leery of arguments that go along the lines of &quot;you just have to accept the social system as it is and not get all uptight about it&quot;, because the underlying subtext is &quot;if you're not a wuss, you'll play out this scene even though you obviously really don't want to&quot;, and that is grade-A nuclear-class bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I didn't phrase it like that. I pointed out it's easy for people to feel attacked in this sort of way, and that the normal response was to place it out of bounds. I also wanted to share a success story at my personal table using the system, because I anticipated player agency/anti-PVP posts like yours being the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:59:11-07:00","id":910471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910212#post910212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So paying your taxes, doing charity that seems to work and at weekends putting on your batsuit and punching some people in the face doesn't seem like that unreasonable a thing to do, given that (assuming we're OK accepting the premise of a man dressing up as a bat and being a vigilante punching criminals in the first place!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for Bill Gates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:16:14-07:00","id":910482,"title":"","content":"Kinda weird. The people I play with never showed any big issue with being convinced to do things by other characters, PC or not. I play like that too, so it made more sense when I played with people who learned RPG with me or from me. But my current group is almost entirely already &quot;RPG grownups&quot; when I met them, and they are fine with it as well. Might have something to do with Vampire, being used to all the intrigue, backstabbing, Presence and Dominate...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:37:27-07:00","id":910491,"title":"","content":"In my experience, to some players the character is an avatar of themselves in the game world, and for others the character is someone they communicate on behalf of. The former tends to take it badly when &quot;they&quot; get influenced, while the latter tends to embrace it (&quot;yeah, that would totally convince this guy, especially if a pretty lady is saying it&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T19:45:58-07:00","id":910498,"title":"","content":"Yes, I find that too. I encourage players that hate their characters being influenced to invest in a lot of Integrity charms. And one PC has invested heavily in Integrity charms (I assume partly for this reason).<br /> <br /> (I say heavily... it's not like there's all that many)<br /> <br /> I do find this is much less of an issue than it was when I started role-playing. I suspect this is because the average age of my play group is over 30 now rather than about 17.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-08-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:05:00-07:00","id":910535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910222#post910222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Unconquered Sun still have virtues in 3E?<br /> Do they influence his exaltation choices?</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect the Virtues are still a philosophical concept that may play into the Unconquered Sun's charms/miracles, and thus still interfere with each other via his choices. I like that plot hook for dealing with him in 2E, and you don't need Virtues as their own stats to keep it in 3E.<br /> <br /> Also the Virtues are the entire reason for his four armed iconography, so I strongly expect they still exist in his purview/theology, even while not being stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T21:34:46-07:00","id":910554,"title":"","content":"Well, insofar as we probably won't be getting actual statistics for the Unconquered Sun in 3rd edition it probably won't matter overly much. That said I suspect that there will still be the idea of the Four Virtues that the Unconquered Sun thinks are pretty cool, and it's occasionally in-vogue in Yu-Shan to claim allegiance to one, and there's even several Martial Art Styles created around them because the idea of explaining existence using these 4 virtues is (or was) popular. But it won't be because these Virtues are a cornerstone of Creation's existence or because the Unconquered Sun is this sort of psuedo-autistic being who is torn between these four battling concepts and has trouble dealing with various real life situations because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T00:57:14-07:00","id":910617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lessens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910142#post910142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It specifically mentions the Bull of the North catapulting livestock fed on human meat into cities as a means of spreading the puppeteer's plague. I'm not sure I would call the Bull of the North a &quot;straight-up&quot; villain, but that's pretty villainous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but I was thinking of Havesh the Vanisher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T01:27:18-07:00","id":910627,"title":"","content":"My definition of &quot;the good guys&quot; in Exalted is pretty lax; basically the groups that don't habitually eat souls, torture souls, drink Soylent Cocacola, make armor out of tortured people, have a religion about wanting to destroy the world, or serve a master that wants to destroy the world. There debatably isn't objective evil in Exalted, but there's a lot of dark otherworldly masters that make serving Orcus or Vecna seem morally defensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:06:47-07:00","id":910642,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't feel like eating or making armor out of souls is that big a deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:08:37-07:00","id":910644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910642#post910642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't feel like eating or making armor out of souls is that big a deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which souls (high or low soul I mean).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T02:49:13-07:00","id":910655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910644#post910644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends which souls (high or low soul I mean).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also depends on <i>whose</i> soul. I mean, if they were going to soulforge your soul into a spittoon, I might not care too much. But if they were planning to do it with <i>my</i> soul, I'm sure I could come up with a long list of reasons why soulforging is an absolutely terrible thing and someone needs to put a stop to it <i>right now.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:27:48-07:00","id":910669,"title":"","content":"Although you will get the occasional ashtray who <i>really </i>deserved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:29:38-07:00","id":910671,"title":"","content":"Solars might not be the good guys, but everyone else is the bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/957-wulfram","name":"Wulfram","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:30:41-07:00","id":910672,"title":"","content":"That's... a bit of a simplification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T03:43:35-07:00","id":910676,"title":"","content":"#NotAllDragonBlooded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:10:22-07:00","id":910721,"title":"","content":"Plus, Lunars and Sidereals.<br /> I mean, yes, Ma-Ha-Suchi, Raksi and Chejop Kejak, sure. But there's plenty of good Lunars and Sidereals. I'd argue the majority (I mean, relatively). They generally want to improve Creation. Most Sidereals, Lunars and Solars will, if they see some kids about to be eaten by Fair Folk or demons, save them. Alchemicals too actually. Most of them do want to improve Creation, and protect it from supernatural threats, they just argue about how. The Lunars' powers encourage brutality and murder, but they are noble savages who care about the world. The Sidereals' powers encourage trickery, and their politics encourage a &quot;do-whatever-it-takes&quot; mentality, &quot;end justifies the means&quot;, but their end aim is to protect the world.<br /> The story of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals isn't about bad people who want to rule the world, it's about great people with noble aims who fight to the death over different views of how the world can be saved. Some may be personally bad, but they're not bad inherently from what they are.<br /> Some of course, do just want to conquer and rule, but for most that's at most a means to the end of fixing the world.<br /> <br /> Whereas the majority of Infernals and Abyssals are bad people with bad aims (though, in 3rd ed, hopefully there are plenty who are good, not just a few).<br /> <br /> As to Dragonblood... they are, as people said, rather mixed. The Dynasty as a whole is evil, but a)not in a simple way, it also does good things, and b)that doesn't mean all its members are evil, and c)only about half of Dragonblood are dynasts, there's another 10,000 outcastes, who occupy the same kind of place as Solars, just more respected and less powerful.<br /> <br /> And finally... I don't think the Alchemicals are evil because they drink soylent cola. I mean, the bodies are dead after all. Cannibalism is repugnant, and dangerous (because of prions) but if you didn't kill the people, I don't see it as necessarily evil. Especially in the low-food environment of Autocthonia.<br /> Actually I often use cannibalism for barbarian characters to show this character's morality is different from others, seeming savage, but they're not actually evil so I don't mind playing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally... I'll be honest, to many of my players, Lunars and Alchemicals have always appeared the most moral. I have one player who won't play Solars, he doesn't like them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-09-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:53:23-07:00","id":910743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910721#post910721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, Lunars and Sidereals.<br /> I mean, yes, Ma-Ha-Suchi, Raksi and Chejop Kejak, sure. But there's plenty of good Lunars and Sidereals. I'd argue the majority (I mean, relatively). They generally want to improve Creation. Most Sidereals, Lunars and Solars will, if they see some kids about to be eaten by Fair Folk or demons, save them. Alchemicals too actually. Most of them do want to improve Creation, and protect it from supernatural threats, they just argue about how. The Lunars' powers encourage brutality and murder, but they are noble savages who care about the world. The Sidereals' powers encourage trickery, and their politics encourage a &quot;do-whatever-it-takes&quot; mentality, &quot;end justifies the means&quot;, but their end aim is to protect the world.<br /> The story of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals isn't about bad people who want to rule the world, it's about great people with noble aims who fight to the death over different views of how the world can be saved. Some may be personally bad, but they're not bad inherently from what they are.<br /> Some of course, do just want to conquer and rule, but for most that's at most a means to the end of fixing the world.<br /> <br /> Whereas the majority of Infernals and Abyssals are bad people with bad aims (though, in 3rd ed, hopefully there are plenty who are good, not just a few).<br /> <br /> As to Dragonblood... they are, as people said, rather mixed. The Dynasty as a whole is evil, but a)not in a simple way, it also does good things, and b)that doesn't mean all its members are evil, and c)only about half of Dragonblood are dynasts, there's another 10,000 outcastes, who occupy the same kind of place as Solars, just more respected and less powerful.<br /> <br /> And finally... I don't think the Alchemicals are evil because they drink soylent cola. I mean, the bodies are dead after all. Cannibalism is repugnant, and dangerous (because of prions) but if you didn't kill the people, I don't see it as necessarily evil. Especially in the low-food environment of Autocthonia.<br /> Actually I often use cannibalism for barbarian characters to show this character's morality is different from others, seeming savage, but they're not actually evil so I don't mind playing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally... I'll be honest, to many of my players, Lunars and Alchemicals have always appeared the most moral. I have one player who won't play Solars, he doesn't like them at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is perfectly moral in-setting for great people to conquer and rule by force, under the assumption that the power gives them the right to rule, and their power will protect the ruled. Average people in the Threshold probably prefer the yoke of the Realm to the uncertainty of warlords and petty kings. The concept of rights is largely foreign, so they just count themselves lucky the Realm garrison keeps bandits away most of the time and only takes 30% of their harvest. Solar/Lunar Alexander the Great believes the world exists to be conquered, and that his rule will bring peace and stability to the world. He prides himself both on his military capabilities and on his willingness to assimilate people into his dominion, rather than enslaving or killing them.<br /> <br /> Creation is also a brutal world. Slaughtering a village of plague victims and their livestock then burning the lot might seem horrible to us, but to the ruler of a small nation in Creation, it's just plain necessary. A Sidereal might mourn the death of a thousand villagers by drowning, but he also knows by breaking the dam when he did he saved ten thousand people. Sometimes hard choices must be made, and it's their job to make them.<br /> <br /> I think the Dynasty is incredibly evil, as a whole, but again we have to take things in context. Dynasts are raised to believe they are spiritually superior, and the world literally belongs to them. They have this status due to their moral rectitude in a past life. Conversely, if someone is a slave, it's because of their moral failings in a past life, period. That sort of upbringing, coupled with extreme privilege (as SLS said, every day is free oral sex day), and then topped off with self-reinforcing peer pressure is going to mold most Dynasts into the kind of people who simply don't see the brutality of what they do. I wouldn't say it excuses their behavior, but it does allow the portrayal of characters who believe in the Dragons and the Realm earnestly and yet are not black-mustached super-villains. From their own in-setting PoV, most Dynasts are fairly moral and loyal scions of the primary source of stability in the world.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what leads your players who use primitive people as disposable shock troops are moral, but the crux of both our posts is morality is fungible within the context of the game, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:08:55-07:00","id":910748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910535#post910535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Virtues are the entire reason for his four armed iconography, so I strongly expect they still exist in his purview/theology, even while not being stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerely doubt that was anything other than a <i>post hoc</i> rationalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:19:41-07:00","id":910757,"title":"","content":"Sure, but I <i>like</i> that rationalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:50:35-07:00","id":910781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what leads your players who use primitive people as disposable shock troops are moral</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they view Lunars as trying to help primitive people and protect them from a rapacious Empire. Which sometimes involves leading them in heroic wars of native resistance.<br /> (I should perhaps note that several of my players are anarchists. I suspect this is related. There's one player who's a liberal: he ironically plays somewhat authoritarian characters, for example at the moment the Queen of a country, which sometimes leads to clashes. The others don't have strong political views. I'm a socialist, but hope it doesn't affect my game: except that I can't stand playing aristocratic heroes, unless they're disgraced or bastards or something. Aristocratic villains are fine of course.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the crux of both our posts is morality is fungible within the context of the game, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to claim that, because it's a good point, and easier to defend. But it wasn't actually what I mean, I must admit.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that, broadly speaking, the majority of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals, and a sizeable number of Dragonblood, have the aim of improving Creation (and another sizeable number of Dragonblood just want . They may disagree about the means, and may do bad things to achieve that, but (again, this in wide generalities), and may interpret it through limited lenses (perhaps fighting for their own tribe), but a world where the Solars, Lunars or Sidereals, as a group (rather than individuals, who may just care about their group), have <i>won</i>, is overall probably a better world than now. They all want to keep the world safe from monsters. Even the Dragonblood also do that (though they have the problem of being aristocrats).<br /> <br /> Whereas the Abyssals (from a 2nd ed perspective) want to destroy the world. And the Infernals want it to damn it to hell and enslave it under mad god-monsters (again, from a 2nd ed perspective).<br /> <br /> Now, you can see there are a lot caveats: this is a generality, doesn't apply to everyone, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> But overall, as a very broad rule, this is how I think of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals: imperfect heroes who fight over different aims and loves, but still heroic. While the Abyssals and Infernals are villains. When Sidereals turn up to murder the PCs, it's because they think the world is better and safer without them, that people will be safer and happier if the PCs are dead. When Abyssals turn up to kill them, it's because they love killing people.<br /> <br /> Essentially, Solars, Lunars, Dragonblood, Alchemicals and Sidereals are <i>supposed</i> to be heroes (in-universe, I don't mean the ST should tell the players they have to be heroes), even if they fail to live up to it. Whereas Abyssals and Infernals are supposed to be villains, and become anti-heroes by rebelling against their nature and purpose.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say this is actually how I run the game: right now, the villains the PCs face are Solars, and they'll later face DBs, Lunars, and maybe Alchemicals, while the local Abyssal circle is friendly and rules the local Underworld peacefully.<br /> <br /> But this is how I think about the setting.<br /> It's perhaps not very nuanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-09-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:00:38-07:00","id":910790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910748#post910748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely doubt that was anything other than a <i>post hoc</i> rationalization.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That symbolism was pretty intentionally there with his 4 objects in Games of Divinity art (the spear, the shield, the trumpet, and the laurel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-09-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:11:41-07:00","id":910799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910617#post910617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, but I was thinking of Havesh the Vanisher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, Havesh the Vanisher is one of my favourite canon Solars. Serial killer who exalted murdering a fat merchant for a few coins. Absolutely hilarious. I love him. I made him King of the Casteless of Varang in my game (under a fake name).<br /> <br /> He's also a perfect example of how much use you can get out of an Essence 1 charm with no prereq charms if you think it all the way through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-09-2016, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:56:31-07:00","id":910845,"title":"","content":"While rewatching some of the Crash Course U.S. history videos, it came to the interesting subject of American industrialists of the 19th century, who are alternatively lauded as captains of history or vilified as robber barons by actual American historiography depending on, as John Green put it &quot;whether we're mad at them&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting aspect of how these things work, where the qualities or achievements that people can find admirable about a historical individual can actually be dependent on them having used methods that were fairly dubious, whether they be exploitation of their workers or ruthless elimination of competitors (in the sense of destroying their capacity to do business, which in some ways, could actually be seen as worse than killing people; it's probably fairly unpleasant to have your life's work destroyed beyond any possibility of recovery and then have to live for another thirty or forty years). Not just as a matter of successful individualism either; resulting developments of industry and finance actually did do a lot to improve the prosperity of that nation, and even though workers had little rights with regards to things like job security or injury compensation, ones who did manage to keep their jobs and not get debilitating injuries would have seen increases in their living standards. Those are all significant as things that create a legacy that many people today benefit from, which probably helps shape the resulting historiography.<br /> <br /> Overall, it might suggest that the standard of heroism the game follows as not as ancient as some people would think.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, all of that stuff about workers also leads back around to the matter of how workers widely organized in pursuit of increasing their rights, often in the face of extreme responses and even violence, which I'd say is a... demonstration of a frequently brought up matter vis a vis &quot;Solars are a lot more powerful than regular people, so regular people have absolutely no recourse to getting Solars to listen to them or effect changes to their benefit as they would define it&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I guess that's another thing that influences the question of whether or not Solars are &quot;good guys&quot;; whether or not one thinks that being powerful, or applying their powers in various ways available to them, would be the kind of thing that would inescapably render the African American Civil Rights Movement a complete wash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serial killer who Exalted murdering a fat merchant</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that's... not really an accurate description of Havesh's mark, and it was more a case of him Exalting while the tough old silversmith was successfully fighting back, but...<br /> <br /> Would you generally equate hired killers with serial killers?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:02:55-07:00","id":910847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910845#post910845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you generally equate hired killers with serial killers?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do on <i>Criminal Minds</i>... &gt;.&gt; &lt;.&lt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:04:17-07:00","id":910849,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean they do kill multiple people, generally one after another, but to be fair that alone being the definition is really iffy because it would also include a lot of soldiers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:13:17-07:00","id":910856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910847#post910847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do on <i>Criminal Minds</i>... &gt;.&gt; &lt;.&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI understand that show once equated &quot;Romani&quot; with &quot;vile mass kidnappers&quot;, soooo....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:15:02-07:00","id":910859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910856#post910856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI understand that show once equated &quot;Romani&quot; with &quot;vile mass kidnappers&quot;, soooo....</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;SERIAL&quot; kidnappers, please. It wasn't &quot;mass.&quot; <br /> (Yes, the show has some issues. I'm being facetious.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:34:54-07:00","id":910938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910790#post910790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That symbolism was pretty intentionally there with his 4 objects in Games of Divinity art (the spear, the shield, the trumpet, and the laurel)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:55:24-07:00","id":910958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910859#post910859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;SERIAL&quot; kidnappers, please. It wasn't &quot;mass.&quot;<br /> (Yes, the show has some issues. I'm being facetious.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI've been watching too much anime lately; I keep looking at this post and my mind automatically says &quot;sou da yo&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it would appear that we're in agreement.<br /> <br /> I mean, being a killer for hire isn't exactly good, but it still... characterizes differently from a serial killer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:21:48-07:00","id":910978,"title":"","content":"I think probably the best distinction when it comes to the 'hired killer' versus 'serial killer' is to recognize one distinction. A hired killer is a mass killer motivated by a contract. As a mass killer, a hired killer has many different kills (individual events of killing). Contract killers will pick their targets according to which contracts come to them, and they'll execute those contracts in whichever manner strikes them as the most effective means of accomplishing their goal with minimal risk of capture or casualty. A serial killer may have many different victims, but they have the SAME kill, that they get better at performing each time. For the serial killer, there's on some level an effort to ritualize and reproduce with refinements the same event. They try to pick the same victim in some sense. They pick a murder method and stick with it, even if it isn't efficient. They feel compelled to revisit places where they've killed. There's a pathology to their actions that you won't find in a hired killer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:06:46-07:00","id":911016,"title":"","content":"Why must so many discussions of Solar morality always circle back to bleeding Havesh? Like, every time.<br /> <br /> PERSON: Are Solars good?<br /> ME: Is any group of people? Solars are GRAND. <br /> PERSON: What about Havesh the Vanisher, tho?<br /> ME: Havesh the Vanisher is pretty damn grand at what he does, but by no measure good. He's a perfectly fine Night Caste.<br /> PERSON: But he's such a big mean jerk! I like Solars but don't like Havesh!<br /> ME: I like Indian people but don't like Narendra Modi. <br /> PERSON: Could Havesh not be a Solar, tho?<br /> ME: SPELL THE ENTIRE WORD &quot;THOUGH&quot; GODDAMN YOU! *stab stab stab stab stab*<br /> PERSON: You... c-can't be a Solar... eitherrrrrr *dead*<br /> <br /> ... what were we talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:21:54-07:00","id":911090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910471#post910471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Works for Bill Gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bat-Gates, he's not the hero we deserve, but he's not the hero that we need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910781#post910781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But overall, as a very broad rule, this is how I think of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals: imperfect heroes who fight over different aims and loves, but still heroic. While the Abyssals and Infernals are villains. When Sidereals turn up to murder the PCs, it's because they think the world is better and safer without them, that people will be safer and happier if the PCs are dead. When Abyssals turn up to kill them, it's because they love killing people.<br /> <br /> Essentially, Solars, Lunars, Dragonblood, Alchemicals and Sidereals are <i>supposed</i> to be heroes (in-universe, I don't mean the ST should tell the players they have to be heroes), even if they fail to live up to it. Whereas Abyssals and Infernals are supposed to be villains, and become anti-heroes by rebelling against their nature and purpose.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say this is actually how I run the game: right now, the villains the PCs face are Solars, and they'll later face DBs, Lunars, and maybe Alchemicals, while the local Abyssal circle is friendly and rules the local Underworld peacefully.<br /> <br /> But this is how I think about the setting.<br /> <br /> It's perhaps not very nuanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I started out reading this and from knowing your posting history, I was a bit like &quot;Eh? Surely I would've expected that when an Abyssal comes to town to take down a group of Solars in his games, it's because they're an actual threat to some empire building, or the Deathlord has compelled the Abyssal, or the Abyssal's ghost troops would rebel or whatnot. Rather than because they like killing and Solar killing is the *best* kind of killing. While for those Sidereals, I would expect it's not necessarily as much whether they truly believe that it is the right thing to do, as not being able to separate this from they are part of a large organisation, that expects them to make that choice.&quot; <br /> <br /> So it's kind of like, I don't even really get the point in thinking much in terms of different intrinsic motivations (villainous and sadistic, noble and well intentioned), if in practice you would say in games it's even more circumstantial factors and varied. Although if it works for you and everything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:22:19-07:00","id":911091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911016#post911016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why must so many discussions of Solar morality always circle back to bleeding Havesh? Like, every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because in a substantive way, the whole reason Havesh exists is to make clear to people that Solars don't have to be lawful good. He's there to give players permission to be bastards... while at the same time pointing out that just because a person has the capacity for greatness doesn't mean they won't piss it away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:31:41-07:00","id":911102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911091#post911091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because in a substantive way, the whole reason Havesh exists is to make clear to people that Solars don't have to be lawful good.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and also because when the Caste books were being written, they wanted one character in each book to represent the &quot;Anathema&quot; concept used by the Dragon Blooded. So the Dawn book had Lyta, who gathers up armies of tiger warriors to spend against the Realm, Zenith had Wind, who is a fallen Immaculate that travels Creation preaching the heresy, Twilight has Fehim, who engages in deals and congress with demons, Night has Havesh who murders for pleasure and hides his true nature, and Eclipse have Mirror Flag who gathers up mobs and shouts revolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:38:09-07:00","id":911107,"title":"","content":"Oh, I <b>get</b> that. My reaction is the reaction of a frequent flier having to sit through the safety course. I don't actually NEED an actual character to serve as proof of what is already obvious. Of course Solars can be bastards. See: Gamesh, Gilbert. Also Achilles. And pretty much everyone in Water Margin. <br /> <br /> The problem with circling back to Havesh is people then come out and say, &quot;But is he REALLY a proper Solar?&quot; &quot;Yes.&quot; &quot;Really?&quot; &quot;Yes.&quot; &quot;Him?&quot; &quot;Yes. Thank you, come again!&quot; He causes more problems than he solves. <br /> <br /> If you NEED a Havesh to show you Solars can be horrible, you're the sort of goober who has a 50% chance to want a mulligan on Havesh in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:38:14-07:00","id":911151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910781#post910781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they view Lunars as trying to help primitive people and protect them from a rapacious Empire. Which sometimes involves leading them in heroic wars of native resistance.<br /> (I should perhaps note that several of my players are anarchists. I suspect this is related. There's one player who's a liberal: he ironically plays somewhat authoritarian characters, for example at the moment the Queen of a country, which sometimes leads to clashes. The others don't have strong political views. I'm a socialist, but hope it doesn't affect my game: except that I can't stand playing aristocratic heroes, unless they're disgraced or bastards or something. Aristocratic villains are fine of course.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to claim that, because it's a good point, and easier to defend. But it wasn't actually what I mean, I must admit.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that, broadly speaking, the majority of Solars, Lunars and Sidereals, and a sizeable number of Dragonblood, have the aim of improving Creation (and another sizeable number of Dragonblood just want . They may disagree about the means, and may do bad things to achieve that, but (again, this in wide generalities), and may interpret it through limited lenses (perhaps fighting for their own tribe), but a world where the Solars, Lunars or Sidereals, as a group (rather than individuals, who may just care about their group), have <i>won</i>, is overall probably a better world than now. They all want to keep the world safe from monsters. Even the Dragonblood also do that (though they have the problem of being aristocrats).<br /> ...<br /> It's perhaps not very nuanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchist, that explains it. I personally have a libertarian-tinged conservative view of things myself, but I don't think it influences my gaming very much. My next PC is going to be hell-bent on conquering a decent chunk of Creation by force, and I tend to win <i>Civilization</i> games by military force more often than not.<br /> <br /> I think the lenses notion you mention is pretty important. To the Lunars of the Caul, Creation will be better when the Realm is expunged from their island. Their people will be safer, they personally will be safer, and they will be one step closer to stopping the &quot;bad guys.&quot; I think you could flip that statement to the perspective of the Dynasty and be in the same position. So, few Exalts think of themselves as villains. Even Havesh and Lyta justify themselves in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Since you mentioned your games, I'll talk about mine. My &quot;villains&quot; are rarely serial killers, conquering warlords, or thieves. They tend to simply be arrogant, selfish, entitled, ambitious, loyal, or myopic. Sometimes they aren't even true villains; they are someone else's hero. That isn't to say I don't use &quot;normal&quot; evil in my games, but more as spice or background flavor. Sure, there's a brutal band of murderous raiders attacking the sand ship every few days, and yes their likes include casual torture and slavery. But, the real story is someone on board is trying to sabotage your ship. Who is it, and what's their motivation?<br /> <br /> For the record, she is totally not a Bronze Faction Chosen of Secrets trying to divert you from unearthing this First Age Library because she would rather not kill everyone on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:46:32-07:00","id":911161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911102#post911102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Havesh who murders for pleasure</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bEhhhhh<br /> [img]\u200bhttps://media.giphy.com/media/5yLgocbquHUTqpzhZ6g/giphy.gif[/img]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:54:29-07:00","id":911170,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I was writing in broad generalities. He murders so he can get his victim's money, their wife, their status, etc. But it's also important to remember that he does actually enjoy killing the sorts of rich and powerful assholes he hated as a mortal, because he likes seeing the fear in their eyes when they realize that there's someone even bigger and more powerful than they are and that their money and power can't protect them. He absolutely enjoys that, and while that isn't typically the sole reason he kills someone (he likes getting shiny shit out of it), it is a motivating factor.<br /> <br /> He's sort of the classic cliche of the guy who used to get bullied and treated like dirt by a group of people, and now that he's bigger and stronger he turns around and bullies them (only in this case he kills them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:58:57-07:00","id":911171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys#post909007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Solars the good guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, they're not infrequently the better guys? &quot;Better&quot; is open to wide interpretation. But yeah, you can have &quot;bad&quot; Solars. A lot of others put it way better than me. I...I just wanted to be involved in the thread!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:58:44-07:00","id":911208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910781#post910781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they view Lunars as trying to help primitive people and protect them from a rapacious Empire. Which sometimes involves leading them in heroic wars of native resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a <i>little</i> more nuanced than that, at least in my case: it's not that Lunars are 'good guys' as such, since I'd regard being a 'good guy' as one of the things that Exalted inherently problematises to begin with [1]. It's more that Lunars, because of the way that they're embedded into the society of the Threshold and the particular MO that they have provide a way of looking at issues of interest to me in a way that Solars generally don't [2]. Also bear in mind that my other favourite PC archetype is the disaffected Dynast...<br /> <br /> [1] Insert joke about the Doctrine of Total Depravity here. Though probably my earlier remarks about King Arthur would be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> [2] Naturally, this means that I'm playing a Solar in Oz's game...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":978,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","user":"Iozz-Sothoth","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:08:40-07:00","id":911218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911170#post911170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's also important to remember that he does actually enjoy killing the sorts of rich and powerful assholes he hated as a mortal, because he likes seeing the fear in their eyes when they realize that there's someone even bigger and more powerful than they are and that their money and power can't protect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI've got to say, as a member of an audience, I often like that kind of thing as well.<br /> <br /> Some of Totentanz's point there about &quot;villainous&quot; characters pinged off of some of my tastes here; when I enjoy heroic narratives, I often like the catharsis of moments in which antagonistic figures who are so cocksure and proud have a dawning moment of realisation that things are suddenly about to stop going their way. It's the kind of thing I often imagine as the moment when people become Solars, and a bit of a summary of what they're in the world for.<br /> <br /> I can't entirely fault a character for that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:40:12-07:00","id":911334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=910845#post910845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's... not really an accurate description of Havesh's mark, and it was more a case of him Exalting while the tough old silversmith was successfully fighting back, but...<br /> <br /> Would you generally equate hired killers with serial killers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant he's a serial killer (present), who exalted killing a guy (past) who didn't deserve it. It's admittedly a while since I read his write-up, so I misremembered the exact details of his victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:46:20-07:00","id":911342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911208#post911208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a <i>little</i> more nuanced than that, at least in my case: it's not that Lunars are 'good guys' as such, since I'd regard being a 'good guy' as one of the things that Exalted inherently problematises to begin with [1]. It's more that Lunars, because of the way that they're embedded into the society of the Threshold and the particular MO that they have provide a way of looking at issues of interest to me in a way that Solars generally don't [2]. Also bear in mind that my other favourite PC archetype is the disaffected Dynast...<br /> <br /> [1] Insert joke about the Doctrine of Total Depravity here. Though probably my earlier remarks about King Arthur would be more appropriate.<br /> <br /> [2] Naturally, this means that I'm playing a Solar in Oz's game...</div> </div> </div> </div>A Solar who likes the Immaculate Order no less!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:59:57-07:00","id":911360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911090#post911090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bat-Gates, he's not the hero we deserve, but he's not the hero that we need.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is where I started out reading this and from knowing your posting history, I was a bit like &quot;Eh? Surely I would've expected that when an Abyssal comes to town to take down a group of Solars in his games, it's because they're an actual threat to some empire building, or the Deathlord has compelled the Abyssal, or the Abyssal's ghost troops would rebel or whatnot. Rather than because they like killing and Solar killing is the *best* kind of killing. While for those Sidereals, I would expect it's not necessarily as much whether they truly believe that it is the right thing to do, as not being able to separate this from they are part of a large organisation, that expects them to make that choice.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it's kind of like, I don't even really get the point in thinking much in terms of different intrinsic motivations (villainous and sadistic, noble and well intentioned), if in practice you would say in games it's even more circumstantial factors and varied. Although if it works for you and everything!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get that it doesn't seem to fit with what I normally say. I mean, I don't actually like using Abyssals who are just &quot;bwahaha, I love murder&quot; because it's extremely boring. Or Solars who are shining paladins. Though I'm happy to have barbaric Lunars and treacherous secret-master Sidereals... though I also like treacherous secret-master Lunars and barbaric Sidereals!<br /> As I said, at the moment the villains are god-hating Solars and their barbarian horde who want to murder the Incarnae, while the local Underworld is ruled peacefully by an Abyssal who is one of the PCs' father.<br /> <br /> How to explain this...<br /> In a very, very, broad, stereotypical sense, I see the Solar host, Lunar host, Five-Score Fellowship and Dragon-blood as the heroes of the game, because their very broad, overall aim is to defend Creation. While Abyssals and Infernals overall aim is to attack Creation.<br /> But then, you start looking closer, and of course actually a lot of it is just self-interested or self-absorbed actors doing their own thing. Because nuance.<br /> Essentially, to deconstruct, you need a starting point.<br /> <br /> Like... most Solar or Dragon-blood villains are the kind of villains who turn up when the superheroes have been defeated to save the Earth from alien invasion, if nothing else because hey, it's where they live (even if previously they may have made deals with the aliens to get one over on the superheroes). Whereas Infernal villains are the ones who are loyal to the aliens.<br /> (Generally: it's not like there aren't Solar Akuma)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is what I think is important about the setting. I have no problem with seeing Abyssals or Infernals who want to save Creation. This is just how the setting appears to me currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:00:56-07:00","id":911361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911334#post911334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant he's a serial killer (present)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHavesh has killed maybe... twice on occasions when he wasn't being paid for it.<br /> <br /> He's also, if not morally, then at least socially discerning in his targets, which puts him a few legs up n Harmonious Jade.<br /> <br /> Hmm, there was a thread a few years back concerning the merits of characters who are assassins in a setting in which life is valued differently to values that would be familiar to our own experiences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">who exalted killing a guy (past) who didn't deserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>{shrug}<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: All right, that's a bit more flippant than I'd like. What I'm finding hard to express is a sense of... not that whether or not he &quot;deserved it&quot; is irrelevant, just that it's a bit... loaded? I don't know.<br /> <br /> I think discussions of Havesh's origins tend to overlook the part where he was impoverished and oppressed and circumstances drew him into an existing network of criminality. Really, it's a significant detail across his entire story; there exist people to commission him as a killer.<br /> <br /> That's not question of him or any similar fictional character or innumerable real people not being morally culpable, just... it's a context that I think is worth noting. I wouldn't say people driven into severe criminality by such a background are wholly blameless, but that it can be a situation of such desperation as I cannot imagine that I cannot wholly condemn.<br /> <br /> It's like Anubis said; the bully who was bullied. Which is to say, the person who was rendered powerless in a manner that normalized such actions for them who tries to feel power by creating powerlessness for others. It doesn't mean they're victimless, but they're still a victim. And there's a limit to which people can not be a product of their environment.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:11:03-07:00","id":911367,"title":"","content":"I also like the idea of Abyssals and Infernals being constructed out of villainous motifs and cosmetics which then get elaborated on in terms following many philosophical and cultural conventions that aren't exactly life-affirming (from a perspective that does not view such things as necessarily bad).<br /> <br /> It's like... use Solars to have the conventional heroic narrative to portray questions of the complexity of power, redressing injustices and pursuing visions for society.<br /> <br /> Use Abyssals to have conventional villainous imagery to portray subjects of the macabre and philosophically elaborate pessimism.<br /> <br /> Use Infernals to have conventional villainous imagery to portray matters of frustration and deviance in the pursuit of catharsis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:43:16-07:00","id":911389,"title":"","content":"I kind of agree, in that I like to use Solars to express the themes of complexity of power, how do you rule a society well, etc.<br /> <br /> While Abyssals are about the themes of death and darkness, definately &quot;dark&quot; themes, but it's not quite so simple as good or evil.<br /> <br /> I also like to use Lunars, while having some of the same themes as Solars, look at savagery vs civilisation, the views of good and evil of alternate cultures (does cannibalism make them evil? What about bestiality?) and so on.<br /> <br /> So yeah, heroic imagery for Solars, villainous imagery for Abyssals and Infernals, which isn't to necessarily say that they are heroes or villains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use Infernals to have conventional villainous imagery to portray matters of frustration and deviance in the pursuit of catharsis. </div> </div> </div>This I'm not so sure about. I've never really been interested as Infernals as deviants, more with Infernals as fundamentally alien to humanity. Which may make them seem evil, but that's what you can discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:55:13-07:00","id":911392,"title":"","content":"As I have said a few times, I think that each type of exalt has themes that are essential to their character and shouldn't be frequently subverted, morality isnt one of them. I agree with the previous posts that Abyssals and Infernals arent inherently 'evil' but that they do use imagery which we traditionally align with villainy, but I tend to think that the second a character is 100% good (like Superman, the dullest character to ever exist no matter how much angst they try to put on him) or 100% evil, they stop being interesting.<br /> <br /> I used to frequently homebrew Deathlords and I never once forgot to give them some redeeming or uncharacteristic trait, they were still 'bad' people but to quote from Guardians of the Galaxy &quot;I don't think anyone is 100% a dick&quot; in fact the main reason that I so frequently homebrewed their lore (never good at mechanics) is that I found most of the canon ones to be so mindlessly evil that they became boring because it was hard to understand being loyal to any save the Silver Prince. Even Atilla the Hun, one of the worst people in history was considered a hard but fair leader to his people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-09-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:55:59-07:00","id":911393,"title":"","content":"Perhaps deviant was not the best word, I just thought it fit the flow better than &quot;angry rock music&quot;, which is a bit significant in my current conception of how Infernals could be fearsome devil-kings in a manner that would plausibly be compelling both in and out of character.<br /> <br /> I don't really care about fundamentally alien, because I think the Exalted are most interesting and playable as examinations of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:57:59-07:00","id":911395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911392#post911392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Superman, the dullest character to ever exist no matter how much angst they try to put on him</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMust resist urge to turn this into a discussion about Superman animated series...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:00:23-07:00","id":911397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911395#post911395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMust resist urge to turn this into a discussion about Superman animated series...</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies if I stepped on toes but in most of his depictions he is a rather one dimensional boy-scout, never saw the animated series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:24:24-07:00","id":911416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911392#post911392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I have said a few times, I think that each type of exalt has themes that are essential to their character and shouldn't be frequently subverted, morality isnt one of them. I agree with the previous posts that Abyssals and Infernals arent inherently 'evil' but that they do use imagery which we traditionally align with villainy, but I tend to think that the second a character is 100% good (like Superman, the dullest character to ever exist no matter how much angst they try to put on him) or 100% evil, they stop being interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's also unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps deviant was not the best word, I just thought it fit the flow better than &quot;angry rock music&quot;, which is a bit significant in my current conception of how Infernals could be fearsome devil-kings in a manner that would plausibly be compelling both in and out of character.<br /> <br /> I don't really care about fundamentally alien, because I think the Exalted are most interesting and playable as examinations of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not they're alien, but their power is alien. Transhuman perhaps?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:28:01-07:00","id":911420,"title":"","content":"Oh, and while I find Superman very dull, I have actually read some pretty good Superman comics. I forget which one of the New 52 it was (there was like 4 Superman comics) but one of them was one where he was a young journalist investigating corruption and crime and then trying to fight it as superman, but finding it difficult to solve problems this way. That was interesting. But then the writers got bored (or maybe there was new writers) and he just went off to punch bad guys.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there are good comics, I think because they give him good writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:16:57-07:00","id":911433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911416#post911416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not they're alien, but their power is alien. Transhuman perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Their power is alien, and if they have anything similar to the &quot;virtue-warping&quot; charms of 2e Infernals, such as Murder is Meat or Intolerable Burning Truths, their power can twist them to have tinges of alien views, but they're still at their heart fundamentally human - just humans given vast power by alien gods. They can use this power to good ends if so inclined; a sword is a sword no matter how strange, and a Solar can use his Shiny Happygolden sword to slaughter innocents and oppress others as readily as to put down tyrants and free the oppressed..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:38:02-07:00","id":911443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911397#post911397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if I stepped on toes but in most of his depictions he is a rather one dimensional boy-scout, never saw the animated series.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <b>you've</b> seen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911367#post911367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like... use Solars to have the conventional heroic narrative to portray questions of the complexity of power, redressing injustices and pursuing visions for society.<br /> <br /> Use Abyssals to have conventional villainous imagery to portray subjects of the macabre and philosophically elaborate pessimism.<br /> <br /> Use Infernals to have conventional villainous imagery to portray matters of frustration and deviance in the pursuit of catharsis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Dragonblooded to have conventional imperialist imagery to portray ideas of culpability, privilege, and responsibility?<br /> <br /> Use Lunars to have conventional barbarous imagery to really examine the people and the things that we consider barbarous?<br /> <br /> Use Alchemicals to have conventional authoritarian and industrial imagery to examine the human's place in the great societal machine?<br /> <br /> I have no idea about the Sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:55:52-07:00","id":911451,"title":"","content":"Solar's are neither good nor evil. Solar's are people capable of incredible deeds, but that doesn't mean they're prone to being good or evil. Just that they do incredible deeds. They are human, and humans come in all flavors. There are likely as many &quot;good&quot; as there are &quot;bad&quot; Solar's in Creation. Most are probably somewhere between the two, neither paragons nor psychopaths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:15:03-07:00","id":911456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911443#post911443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That <b>you've</b> seen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Use Dragonblooded to have conventional imperialist imagery to portray ideas of culpability, privilege, and responsibility?<br /> <br /> Use Lunars to have conventional barbarous imagery to really examine the people and the things that we consider barbarous?<br /> <br /> Use Alchemicals to have conventional authoritarian and industrial imagery to examine the human's place in the great societal machine?<br /> <br /> I have no idea about the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals can convey necessary treachery, sacrifice and well-intentioned manipulation better than most Exalts I think since they seem to try the hardest to keep Creation going. They are few in number so their comcerns are necesarily more 'global' than most and they are ironically enough the best connected outsiders ever since they are less likely to die young and so more likely to outlive everyone they ever know while being doomed to be forgotten by the world they try to protect. Sidereals embody both traditional assassins and politicians, both careers that are romanticized and hated in equal measure which slowly break you down as you are forced to do what is 'necesary' even as you try to justify to yourself that you arent a complete monster. Heck, they are tragic figures in a very modern way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-10-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:00:01-07:00","id":911546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911416#post911416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not they're alien, but their power is alien.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bMaybe, but I don't want to play their power.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:26:03-07:00","id":911555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911546#post911546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMaybe, but I don't want to play their power.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>For most exalts you shouldn't want to play their power, their power just enables you to play certain characters. Infernals alien side to their power can give you characters like the ones that you find in sci-fi and fantasy, who've been given some strange ability that's normally really horrible, but maybe they can use it for other means. Like those stories where somebody has a demon or an alien bonded to them, which enables them to peer into other's souls or melt their face off with acid or something. You've become almost anathema to yourself, so you can fight it, you can embrace it, or you can try to work with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T03:42:41-07:00","id":911562,"title":"","content":"Something that I think might inform assessments of the morality of the Solar Exalted and their equivalents is...<br /> <br /> I think the folk hero is a major source of the &quot;conventional&quot; heroic narrative that I find the Solar imagery to be constructed from, and one interesting detail I've seen in descriptions of the folk hero is that they typically start out as ordinary people who are then made extraordinary by some kind of significant life event, often harmful such as a disaster or social injustice.<br /> <br /> I consider that against many origins writers have given to Solar Exalted, and it makes me think that a common element between them might be a certain scenario of <i>desperation</i>; something weighing down on them that some part would want to overcome. I think it's part of what can go into assumptions that people Chosen by the Unconquered Sun will pursue some form of renewal for the world; the comfortably powerful don't (often) get Chosen, regardless of their assets or ambitions.<br /> <br /> I would not say that everything people might do from a starting position of desperation is excused or justified, but I think it would be worth noting.<br /> <br /> I find it similar to what seems to be the origin for Abyssals, and what I'm positing as an origin for Infernals, and I find it to be something that would make the relationship with and contrast to Solars more meaningful than any inversion of powers or cosmetics would, and it's something I think skews whatever their &quot;villainous&quot; narratives might be.<br /> <br /> I think particularly for the idea of &quot;the Yozis only have a few Essences, so they would be discerning enough to seek out only the most evil people&quot;, because I wonder what such people would be like. It makes me think of what Totentanz described, the privileged and the arrogant and the myopic; people who are perceived to be evil because they already hold and abuse power over others. I think if such people were given such power, they wouldn't really do anything interesting with it, because there's no urgency in their lives; I would see that as a scenario in which power is used mostly to secure what one already possesses, and then sit on it.<br /> <br /> I imagine Yozis scouring through the ranks of the desperate, the subaltern, the crushed, the <b>vengeful</b>, people for whom being bestowed the power of a god would be very catalysing, and I think the results would be a lot more interesting and to the purposes of the Yozis as I postulate them.<br /> <br /> From that position, with regards to the subject of things like their shintais...<br /> <br /> I've talked at length about how I dislike &quot;power&quot; being used as a metric for characters, because it's often vague and undefined. That's related to how I've often disliked stories that describe a character as having &quot;powers&quot; (especially for the plural), in which we don't necessarily see them do many things.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about Solar Charms is how a lot of them can be behind an action without being visual, in a manner that unifies a turn of phrase I'm a bit attached to with an application in which it makes sense.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, as another contrast with Solars and demonstration of their own thesis, I like the idea that their growth in power <i>would</i> be very visual and diverse. It's still not about the acquisition of power being the main thing they're driven by, but rather that as any given Infernal progresses along their narrative, they do become more powerful and those greater and more diverse powers further enable them to pursue what they want. So to me, the potential of something like shintais isn't that they're alien or make the Exalt alien, but that they're a very visual display of how far they've come and what new capabilities they have to go further.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I don't think I'm explaining that as well as I'd like, and this post is already running rather long...<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll come back to it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T04:27:28-07:00","id":911572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911443#post911443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Dragonblooded to have conventional imperialist imagery to portray ideas of culpability, privilege, and responsibility?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure... I mean, the imperialism is a thing that they do, but it's not what's <i>in</i> them.<br /> <br /> I think they're more a case of...<br /> <br /> The Dragon Blooded of the Realm are an aristocracy that is founded on the fact that their family background literally conveys powers to them. That aristocracy, with its martial connotations, is at the root of their imperialism, so it could be played in stories to examine it, but I think core details of the Dragon Blooded are the experience of being born into power, as well as that power itself being something that is wild and needs to be disciplined.<br /> <br /> I think the stories of the other Exalted might be more about experiencing things than examining things.<br /> <br /> So you've got Lunars who are driven to escape their bonds and pursue various kinds of freedom, and Liminals who are about uncertainty of identity and alienation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:20:59-07:00","id":911634,"title":"","content":"In general, Solars and other Exalts can be heroes or villains, but all are Protagonists, beings who define their own path with struggle and will. If they are blessed or damned, it is by their own hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:06:09-07:00","id":911658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911562#post911562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've talked at length about how I dislike &quot;power&quot; being used as a metric for characters, because it's often vague and undefined. That's related to how I've often disliked stories that describe a character as having &quot;powers&quot; (especially for the plural), in which we don't necessarily see them do many things.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about Solar Charms is how a lot of them can be behind an action without being visual, in a manner that unifies a turn of phrase I'm a bit attached to with an application in which it makes sense.<br /> <br /> For Infernals, as another contrast with Solars and demonstration of their own thesis, I like the idea that their growth in power <i>would</i> be very visual and diverse. It's still not about the acquisition of power being the main thing they're driven by, but rather that as any given Infernal progresses along their narrative, they do become more powerful and those greater and more diverse powers further enable them to pursue what they want. So to me, the potential of something like shintais isn't that they're alien or make the Exalt alien, but that they're a very visual display of how far they've come and what new capabilities they have to go further.<br /> <br /> Hmm, I don't think I'm explaining that as well as I'd like, and this post is already running rather long...<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll come back to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Infernal preview had Infernals buying Ability Charms in order to pick up unique non-Ability powers like Mind-Hand Manipulation and shintai. I kind of would like to see them happen in reverse, where Infernals buy things like Mind-Hand or Verdant Emptiness Endowment and then buy Ability-based Charms that expand on those powers (probably on some kind of increasing cost scheme like their Excellencies used to have so that most Infernals only have two or three base powers).<br /> <br /> Admittedly that seems likely to drive right back into some of their old design weaknesses, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:06:43-07:00","id":911659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911218#post911218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI've got to say, as a member of an audience, I often like that kind of thing as well.<br /> <br /> Some of Totentanz's point there about &quot;villainous&quot; characters pinged off of some of my tastes here; when I enjoy heroic narratives, I often like the catharsis of moments in which antagonistic figures who are so cocksure and proud have a dawning moment of realisation that things are suddenly about to stop going their way. It's the kind of thing I often imagine as the moment when people become Solars, and a bit of a summary of what they're in the world for.<br /> <br /> I can't entirely fault a character for that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Dynast whipping a slave and sees a Castemark ignite on the slave's forehead is having a terrible, horrible, no-good, very bad day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:09:47-07:00","id":911772,"title":"","content":"#DatUsurpationMoment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:06:24-07:00","id":911811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/909007-are-solars-the-good-guys?p=911016#post911016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why must so many discussions of Solar morality always circle back to bleeding Havesh? Like, every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes it comes back to Filial Wisdom or Lyta.<br /> ,<br /> Havesh resonates in a particular way because he's a literal murder hobo. Who after killing you, will briefly steal your life, down to sleeping with your spouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}